[stderr] +---
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Objective
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Define the semantic, responsive web/PWA game-shell contract around the shared
[stderr] +session and game state. It specifies labelled navigation, panel/focus routing,
[stderr] +viewport profiles, reflow, and non-colour cues without creating a PWA-specific
[stderr] +UI, final presentation assets, or fixed device-support claim.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Dependencies
[stderr] +
[stderr] +R0010 supplies the shared accessibility foundation and R0021 supplies session
[stderr] +and checkpoint presentation state. This shell consumes their public states and
[stderr] +routes panels to them without changing their APIs. GATE-0002 remains an
[stderr] +implementation gate for numeric/browser-device thresholds and GATE-0004
[stderr] +remains a gate for final content and layout choices.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Ownership
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- `src/app/shell/`, `src/platform/web/layout/`, and `tests/app/shell/`.
[stderr] +- Semantic navigation, viewport profiles, and panel/focus routing API.
[stderr] +- Title, main controls, status, temporary panels, dialogs, visible focus, and
[stderr] +  responsive reflow rules around shared game state.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Required behaviour
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Provide semantic landmarks for title navigation, main game controls, objective
[stderr] +or status, and dialogs. The game view is the primary workspace; Quest, Bag,
[stderr] +Party, Save, Settings, Help, privacy/diagnostics, and PWA status are labelled
[stderr] +temporary panels with a visible title, close control, and known return target.
[stderr] +Icons always have adjacent text or an accessible name. Title actions reflect
[stderr] +R0021 availability rather than promising unavailable save actions.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Panel changes preserve prior selection and scroll position where practical.
[stderr] +Closing returns focus to the invoking control; a newly opened non-modal panel
[stderr] +receives focus at its heading. Blocking dialogs describe consequences and use a
[stderr] +safe Cancel default. Browser Back closes a transient panel before any leave
[stderr] +prompt, and navigation may not silently discard recoverable progress.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Define narrow, medium, and wide profiles. Narrow layouts use safe-area-aware
[stderr] +world presentation, an expandable objective summary, reachable actions, and
[stderr] +full-screen panels with sticky close/back controls. Medium layouts retain a
[stderr] +primary world with contextual side or bottom panel; wide layouts use a centred
[stderr] +stage with a collapsible status rail and may use two-column inspection. Resize,
[stderr] +rotation, zoom, virtual keyboards, and PWA display-mode changes preserve game
[stderr] +state and selection where practical; if reflow obscures selection, focus moves
[stderr] +to the panel heading and announces the change.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Keep visible focus, labels, state text, and non-colour cues available across
[stderr] +profiles. Touch-operable controls retain the specified target/separation
[stderr] +contract; hover is optional enrichment. Text scaling, contrast, typography,
[stderr] +motion, and exact threshold verification remain governed by R0010 and the
[stderr] +unresolved GATE-0002 rather than being inferred here.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Web and PWA differences
[stderr] +
[stderr] +The responsive web shell and installed PWA consume the same semantic UI,
[stderr] +navigation, session state, and shared campaign rules. PWA display-mode reflow
[stderr] +uses the same profiles, not a forked UI. Installation, service workers, cache
[stderr] +refresh, update activation, and a final support matrix are outside this
[stderr] +contract and remain gated.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Non-goals
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Do not produce final art, fonts, UI assets, campaign content, audio, a fixed
[stderr] +browser/device matrix, service-worker behaviour, cache/update implementation,
[stderr] +or a duplicate PWA interface. Do not resolve GATE-0002 or GATE-0004.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Asset assessment
[stderr] +
[stderr] +`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: semantic shell and layout rules create no
[stderr] +visual/source asset. Do not create or reserve icons, fonts, mockups,
[stderr] +illustrations, or other product assets; `asset_ids` remains blank.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Audio assessment
[stderr] +
[stderr] +`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: this shell contract owns no cue selection,
[stderr] +playback, or mix. Keep all audio metadata blank/default and create no audio
[stderr] +asset.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Verification
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- Use representative session and viewport fixtures to prove labelled controls,
[stderr] +  legal focus order, panel return targets, and safe dialog defaults through
[stderr] +  resize and panel changes.
[stderr] +- Prove narrow, medium, and wide profiles retain all required controls without
[stderr] +  hover-only operation or a PWA-specific UI branch; test reflow focus recovery.
[stderr] +- Compare metadata, requirements, provenance, dependencies, and ownership to
[stderr] +  IMP-0022 and the manifest; retain GATE-0002 and GATE-0004 without treating
[stderr] +  documentation as approval.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Evidence
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Retain semantic-tree/focus traces, viewport and panel fixtures, PWA/web parity
[stderr] +comparison, metadata comparison, and the unresolved gate records.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Acceptance criteria
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- The shell supplies semantic navigation, labelled panels, safe dialog and
[stderr] +  focus routing, and responsive profiles around shared game state.
[stderr] +- Web and installed PWA share one UI contract; no PWA-specific interface,
[stderr] +  support-matrix claim, or lifecycle implementation is introduced.
[stderr] +- GATE-0002 and GATE-0004 remain explicit implementation gates.
