[stderr] +remains an implementation gate for concrete campaign assumptions.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Ownership
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- `src/app/session/` and `tests/app/session/`.
[stderr] +- Session and checkpoint view state, session intents, and safe-boundary API.
[stderr] +- Translation of confirmed persistence/campaign outcomes into an honest player
[stderr] +  session state.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Required behaviour
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Model the lifecycle as `launching → title → new-or-resume → playing ↔ paused →
[stderr] +ending → title`. Expose title actions only when available: without a valid
[stderr] +save, Continue and Load are absent or disabled with an explanation while New
[stderr] +game remains available. Resume starts only from a validated safe boundary.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Pause blocks world and combat advancement. A focus-loss intent safely pauses,
[stderr] +or first reaches an existing safe state where immediate pause is unsafe, and
[stderr] +records a once-per-session explanation for the presentation layer. Repeated
[stderr] +focus-loss, pause, resume, launch, and ending intents are idempotent and may
[stderr] +not duplicate rewards, campaign transitions, or save work.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Represent checkpoint status separately from a request or in-progress save.
[stderr] +Present a checkpoint as confirmed only after R0004 reports successful atomic
[stderr] +confirmation. Interrupted, failed, corrupt, or quarantined saves preserve the
[stderr] +last valid confirmed checkpoint and surface retry, return-to-title, and
[stderr] +fallback/new-game routes supplied by R0006. The session state must never imply
[stderr] +that unconfirmed work, an arbitrary combat moment, or remote data can resume.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Web and PWA differences
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Web and installed-PWA adapters consume the same session intents and confirmed
[stderr] +checkpoint state. Browser visibility hooks, service-worker/cache refresh,
[stderr] +installation prompts, update activation, viewport layout, and storage-driver
[stderr] +selection are adapter work and remain outside this shared model. An update may
[stderr] +be presented only at an existing save-safe title or paused-menu boundary; this
[stderr] +contract does not implement that lifecycle.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Non-goals
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Do not implement browser lifecycle listeners, cache refresh, service workers,
[stderr] +new save schemas, storage drivers, network services, account/sync, UI layout,
[stderr] +content, assets, audio, or a product gate approval. Do not resolve GATE-0003
[stderr] +or GATE-0004.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Asset assessment
[stderr] +
[stderr] +`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: session and checkpoint state requires no
[stderr] +product visual or source asset. Do not create or reserve maps, sprites, icons,
[stderr] +fonts, illustrations, or other assets; `asset_ids` remains blank.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Audio assessment
[stderr] +
[stderr] +`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: this contract selects no cue or playback
[stderr] +behaviour. Keep audio IDs, brief, duration, loop policy, and style version
[stderr] +blank/default; do not create incidental audio.
[stderr] +
