## Objective

Create only R0021–R0023 from the B0009 manifest assignments. Retain all
implementation gates; writing a runbook does not approve implementation.

## Context packet

Read the assigned manifest and catalogue records, the SHARD-03 specification
sections, F014, and the runbook template.

## Output list

- `../runbooks/R0021.md` through `../runbooks/R0023.md`, one per assigned IMP.

## Validation procedure

Confirm metadata, provenance, ownership, dependencies, asset/audio assessment,
and canonical requirement links match the manifest before each write.

## Checkpoint and update procedure

Record only B0009's completed output state after each validated R file. Retain
reserved IDs and repair only the failed output if validation fails.

## Collision protection

Stop if an assigned ID/path is owned by another contract or an accepted file
would be overwritten.

## Stop condition

Stop after R0021–R0023; do not create B0010 outputs or allocate further IDs.

## Acceptance criteria

- Exactly the three assigned R-series files are authored with their manifest mappings.
- Each output retains gates and has complete provenance and asset/audio metadata.
- Structural validation succeeds without overwriting accepted work.
