c/app/input/\",\n      \"tests/platform/input/\"\n    ],\n    \"data\": [\n      \"input binding and availability state\"\n    ],\n    \"api\": [\n      \"semantic input action API\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"forbidden_scope\": [\n    \"native clients\",\n    \"voice recognition\",\n    \"arbitrary remapping guarantee\",\n    \"input-specific rules\"\n  ],\n  \"verification\": \"Fixtures prove equivalent semantic actions, no duplicate destructive confirmation, and usable fallback after gamepad disconnect.\",\n  \"human_external_gate\": \"GATE-0002 remains for approved browser/device compatibility claims.\",\n  \"complexity\": \"high\",\n  \"status\": \"ready_for_authoring\"\n}\n---\ntask_id: B0009\nsequence: 13\ntitle: Author session, shell, and input implementation contracts\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\nplaywright_spec:\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nCreate only R0021\u2013R0023 from the B0009 manifest assignments. Retain all\nimplementation gates; writing a runbook does not approve implementation.\n\n## Context packet\n\nRead the assigned manifest and catalogue records, the SHARD-03 specification\nsections, F014, and the runbook template.\n\n## Output list\n\n- `../runbooks/R0021.md` through `../runbooks/R0023.md`, one per assigned IMP.\n\n## Validation procedure\n\nConfirm metadata, provenance, ownership, dependencies, asset/audio assessment,\nand canonical requirement links match the manifest before each write.\n\n## Checkpoint and update procedure\n\nRecord only B0009's completed output state after each validated R file. Retain\nreserved IDs and repair only the failed output if validation fails.\n\n## Collision protection\n\nStop if an assigned ID/path is owned by another contract or an accepted file\nwould be overwritten.\n\n## Stop condition\n\nStop after R0021\u2013R0023; do not create B0010 outputs or allocate further IDs.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Exactly the three assigned R-series files are authored with their manifest mappings.\n- Each output retains gates and has complete provenance and asset/audio metadata.\n- Structural validation succeeds without overwriting accepted work.\n---\ntask_id: R0017\nsequence: 17\ntitle: Specify campaign progression and safe ending integration\ndependencies: R0013,R0014,R0015,R0016\nrequirement_ids: REQ-0001,REQ-0002,REQ-0003,REQ-0004,REQ-0005\nsource_specifications: specification/02-feature-model.md#2-exploration-town-dungeon-and-campaign-content,specification/02-feature-model.md#3-narrative-quests-onboarding-and-ending\nsource_catalogue_ids: IMP-0017\nauthoring_batch: B0008\nfactory_stages: F011,F012,F013\nasset_impact: not_applicable\nasset_ids:\nasset_brief: No authored campaign expression; integration rules only.\naudio_impact: not_applicable\naudio_ids:\naudio_brief:\naudio_duration_seconds: 0\naudio_loop: not_applicable\naudio_style_version:\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\nplaywright_spec:\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nSpecify the shared-core integration that joins the abstract town-to-dungeon\nroute, required quest/tutorial progress, encounter rewards, and protected\ninventory into one safely completable campaign ending. It owns integration\nrules, not authored story or presentation.\n\n## Dependencies\n\nR0013 owns scene transitions, R0014 owns quest and tutorial transitions, R0015\nowns encounter/reward resolution, and R0016 owns inventory/party safety. This\ncontract composes their public outcomes without transferring their ownership.\nGATE-0004 remains an implementation gate for concrete campaign content.\n\n## Ownership\n\n- `src/core/campaign/progression*` and `tests/core/campaign/progression*`.\n- Campaign route graph, integration checkpoints, completion-state envelope,\n  and the campaign-completion command.\n- Cross-domain ordering rules from validated route through ending completion.\n\n## Required behaviour\n\nAccept completion only when a validated route has reached the authorised final\nstate: legal scene transition, required quest progression, resolved required\nencounter/reward outcome, and protected-item predicates must all hold. Validate\nexpected revision and completion eligibility before mutation. Completion emits\none stable result and is idempotent: a duplicate or stale completion request\nreturns the recorded result without replaying grants, transitions, or ending\neffects. Invalid, blocked, or dead-end routes preserve state with typed\nrejection; optional rewards cannot be completion prerequisites.\n\n## Web and PWA differences\n\nWeb and installed-PWA adapters submit the same completion command and render\nits state/event. Ending UI, navigation, animation, cache updates, persistence,\nand installation lifecycle are outside this shared-core contract.\n\n## Non-goals\n\nDo not author town/dungeon maps, characters, dialogue, ending text, assets,\naudio, UI, extra regions, branching stories, remote content, or save drivers.\nDo not resolve GATE-0004.\n\n## Asset assessment\n\n`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: this is a content-neutral integration\ncontract. Do not create or reserve maps, illustrations, sprites, textures,\nportraits, icons, fonts, or other product assets; `asset_ids` remains blank.\n\n## Audio assessment\n\n`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: the contract does not select, trigger, or\nmix music or sound effects. Keep all audio fields blank/default and do not\ncreate incidental cues.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Use deterministic abstract fixtures to prove exactly one start-to-ending\n  route is reachable only after required cross-domain predicates hold.\n- Prove blocked routes, stale commands, and duplicate completion requests\n  preserve state or return the recorded completion result; no reward repeats.\n- Compare metadata, requirements, ownership, provenance, and dependencies to\n  IMP-0017 and its manifest allocation; retain GATE-0004 explicitly.\n\n## Evidence\n\nRetain reachability output, rejection and duplicate-completion fixtures, the\nmanifest/catalogue comparison, and the unresolved GATE-0004 record.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- One validated abstract route reaches campaign completion without a dead end.\n- Ending completion is revision-checked and idempotent; duplicate effects and\n  reward grants cannot occur.\n- Concrete authored content, UI, assets, audio, and GATE-0004 approval remain\n  outside this contract.\n---\ntask_id: R0018\nsequence: 18\ntitle: Define original campaign content-package and provenance assembly\ndependencies: R0005,R0011,R0013,R0014,R0015,R0016\nrequirement_ids: REQ-0001,REQ-0002,REQ-0008,NFR-0007,NFR-0008\nsource_specifications: specification/02-feature-model.md#2-exploration-town-dungeon-and-campaign-content,specification/02-feature-model.md#3-narrative-quests-onboarding-and-ending,specification/03-technical-contract.md#versioned-content-and-save-schemas\nsource_catalogue_ids: IMP-0018\nauthoring_batch: B0008\nfactory_stages: F011,F012,F013\nasset_impact: required\nasset_ids: ASSET-CAMPAIGN-TOWN,ASSET-CAMPAIGN-DUNGEON,ASSET-CAMPAIGN-CHARACTERS\nasset_brief: Reserve original campaign asset groups for later approved implementation; authoring creates no asset.\nvisual_style_version: unselected-gate-0004\naudio_impact: not_applicable\naudio_ids:\naudio_brief:\naudio_duration_seconds: 0\naudio_loop: not_applicable\naudio_style_version:\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\nplaywright_spec:\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nDefine assembly of one versioned original campaign package that references the\ntown, dungeon, and character asset groups and connects the SHARD-02 domain\ncontracts to the existing content and provenance controls. Reserve assets only;\ndo not create product expression during authoring.\n\n## Dependencies\n\nR0005 owns schema, validation, registry, and package loading. R0011 owns the\nprovenance record and mandatory human creative-review disposition. R0013\u2013R0016\nprovide the content-neutral domain contracts referenced by the package. This\ncontract assembles their allowed references without changing their owners.\nGATE-0004 and the human provenance review block implementation/admission of\nconcrete authored content; neither is resolved here.\n\n## Ownership\n\n- `content/campaign/`, `assets/source-manifest.*`, and\n  `tests/content/campaign*`.\n- Campaign package assembly, stable content references, and provenance-manifest\n  entries for the reserved asset groups.\n- Content package loader integration using the R0005 validation boundary.\n\n## Required behaviour\n\nAssemble a versioned package for exactly one town, one dungeon, and the\ncampaign's character/content references. Every expressive package entry must\nhave a stable content ID, package reference, and complete provenance record as\ndefined by R0011. The loader admits only a package whose references resolve,\nwhose provenance is complete, and whose human creative-review disposition is\nrecorded as ready; it must reject missing, unmatched, or unreviewed entries.\nThe package must use the predecessor contracts' stable IDs rather than define\nnew gameplay rules. A reviewer may hold or reject the package; automated checks\ncannot claim creative, legal, licensing, or GATE-0004 approval.\n\n## Web and PWA differences\n\nThe same validated package is consumed by web and installed-PWA adapters.\nRendering, responsive presentation, packaging, caching, and download behavior\nremain owned by later UI/PWA work and do not bypass provenance validation.\n\n## Non-goals\n\nDo not create, generate, source, select, or approve artwork, maps, characters,\ndialogue, localisation, music, sound effects, licences, or copied expression.\nDo not add regions, UI, PWA delivery, or legal approval; do not resolve\nGATE-0004 or the human review.\n\n## Asset assessment\n\n`asset_impact` is `required`. Reserve only these stable product asset groups:\n`ASSET-CAMPAIGN-TOWN` (one original town environment),\n`ASSET-CAMPAIGN-DUNGEON` (one original dungeon environment), and\n`ASSET-CAMPAIGN-CHARACTERS` (original campaign character expression). They\nappear only through package references and provenance entries; their source of\ntruth is the later approved asset/content implementation. Required variants,\nvisual style, and original-art acceptance remain unselected under\n`unselected-gate-0004`. Authoring creates no files or product assets. Before\nadmission, each eventual asset must have complete provenance and an explicit\nhuman creative-review disposition; technical validation is not approval.\n\n## Audio assessment\n\n`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: no campaign cue is selected or integrated\nby this assembly contract. Keep audio IDs, brief, duration, loop policy, and\nstyle version blank/default; do not create incidental audio.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Validate a synthetic, non-product package whose town/dungeon/character\n  references resolve through R0005 and whose domain references are stable.\n- Prove absent provenance, unmatched references, invalid disposition, or a\n  package not marked ready after human review is rejected before admission.\n- Check that the three reserved IDs, asset brief, and style placeholder match\n  IMP-0018 and the manifest, with no asset created; retain GATE-0004 and the\n  recorded human provenance-review requirement.\n\n## Evidence\n\nRetain package-validator results, rejected provenance fixtures, the synthetic\nhuman-review disposition, asset-reservation comparison, and both gate records.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- The versioned package resolves only validated, stable campaign references.\n- Every expressive entry requires complete provenance and a recorded human\n  creative-review disposition before admission.\n- Only the three manifest-defined asset IDs are reserved; no product asset,\n  copied expression, or creative/legal approval is created or claimed.\n---\ntask_id: R0019\nsequence: 19\ntitle: Add campaign domain invariant and negative-fixture coverage\ndependencies: R0013,R0014,R0015,R0016\nrequirement_ids: REQ-0002,REQ-0003,REQ-0004,NFR-0007\nsource_specifications: specification/02-feature-model.md#2-exploration-town-dungeon-and-campaign-content,specification/02-feature-model.md#4-party-combat-encounters-rewards-and-balance\nsource_catalogue_ids: IMP-0019\nauthoring_batch: B0008\nfactory_stages: F011,F012,F013\nasset_impact: not_applicable\nasset_ids:\nasset_brief: No assets; deterministic invalid-state fixtures only.\naudio_impact: not_applicable\naudio_ids:\naudio_brief:\naudio_duration_seconds: 0\naudio_loop: not_applicable\naudio_style_version:\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\nplaywright_spec:\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nAdd deterministic shared-core negative fixtures and cross-domain invariants for\nthe SHARD-02 campaign contracts. The work proves that invalid references,\nblocked routes, stale commands, and duplicate grants are detected without\nintroducing concrete campaign content.\n\n## Dependencies\n\nR0013 supplies scene/exit validation, R0014 quest transitions, R0015 encounter\nand reward resolution, and R0016 inventory/party protection. This contract owns\nfixtures and invariant assertions only; it does not change their APIs or state\nrules. GATE-0004 remains explicit for concrete content assumptions.\n\n## Ownership\n\n- `tests/core/campaign/fixtures/` and `tests/core/campaign/invariants*`.\n- Deterministic negative campaign fixtures and fixture builders.\n- Cross-contract invariant assertions and repeat-safety coverage.\n\n## Required behaviour\n\nProvide deterministic fixture builders for unresolved scene, quest, encounter,\nreward, item, predicate, and route references; blocked and dead-end routes;\nstale revisions; and duplicate interaction/reward IDs. Each fixture has a\nstable expected rejection or invariant result. Assert that invalid inputs never\nmutate campaign state, required completion routes remain reachable in valid\nabstract fixtures, and retries do not duplicate rewards or progression. Keep\nfixtures content-neutral and isolated from player data.\n\n## Web and PWA differences\n\nThese are shared-core test fixtures. They do not test browser rendering, input,\nresponsive UI, service workers, cache behavior, or installed-PWA lifecycle.\n\n## Non-goals\n\nDo not create product maps, dialogue, characters, combatants, assets, audio,\nreal player data, browser-matrix tests, UI, persistence drivers, or concrete\ncontent values. Do not resolve GATE-0004.\n\n## Asset assessment\n\n`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: deterministic invalid-state fixtures require\nno product visual/source asset. Do not create or reserve maps, sprites, icons,\ntextures, portraits, fonts, or other incidental assets; `asset_ids` is blank.\n\n## Audio assessment\n\n`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: fixtures own no music or sound-effect\ntrigger. Keep audio metadata blank/default and do not create test or product\ncues.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Run every fixture twice and prove byte-for-byte equivalent result, including\n  unchanged state for invalid reference, blocked route, and stale-command cases.\n- Prove duplicate interaction/reward IDs never apply twice and a valid abstract\n  fixture has a reachable completion path with no protected-item dead end.\n- Compare requirements, dependencies, ownership, and provenance against\n  IMP-0019 and the manifest; retain GATE-0004 for concrete assumptions.\n\n## Evidence\n\nRetain deterministic fixture output, invariant failures/rejections, repeat-run\ncomparison, reachability output, and manifest/catalogue comparison.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Every invalid campaign reference and blocked route has deterministic detected\n  coverage and does not mutate state.\n- Valid abstract progression has no dead end; stale commands and duplicate\n  grants are repeat-safe.\n- Fixtures introduce no player data, browser coverage, product assets, audio,\n  or concrete content, while GATE-0004 remains explicit.\n\nexec\n/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^## (1'\"\\\\. Game shell|Information architecture|Layout, visual|Input and interaction|Empty, error)' projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/02-feature-model.md projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/04-experience-contract.md\nrg -n 'GATE-000[234]|REQ-000[5679]|REQ-0010|NFR-000[234]' projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/02-feature-model.md projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/04-experience-contract.md | sed -n '1,160p'\" in /Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator\n succeeded in 0ms:\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/04-experience-contract.md:11:## Information architecture and navigation\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/04-experience-contract.md:46:## Layout, visual tokens, and responsive behaviour\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/04-experience-contract.md:68:## Input and interaction adaptation\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/04-experience-contract.md:94:## Empty, error, recovery, destructive, and privacy-sensitive states\n\nexec\n/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,170p' projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/04-experience-contract.md\nrg -n 'Game shell|session|responsive presentation|GATE-0003|GATE-0004|REQ-0005|REQ-0006' projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/02-feature-model.md | sed -n '1,100p'\nsed -n '1,150p' projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/02-feature-model.md\" in /Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator\n succeeded in 0ms:\n# 04 \u2014 Experience and accessibility contract\n\n**Inputs:** [product brief](01-product-brief.md), [feature model](02-feature-model.md), and [technical, data, trust, and quality contract](03-technical-contract.md). This is the experience contract for the P0 offline campaign: one town, one dungeon, turn-based combat, inventory, quests, saves, settings, and a short ending. It specifies behaviour and presentation without choosing an engine, a library, exact art assets, or an unapproved connected service.\n\n## Experience premise and originality boundary\n\nThe player arrives as a wayfinder in **Larkspur Reach**, a small hillside town whose old beacon has gone dark. A local request leads through the nearby **Glassroot Hollow** to relight it. This is a compact, hopeful mystery about attention, repair, and returning safely\u2014not a borrowed world, cast, plot, place, or visual identity. The ending is a quiet return to the town with the beacon restored and the campaign marked complete.\n\nThe visual language is original: warm hand-painted fantasy with broad, readable silhouettes; worn clay, moss, lantern-gold, plum shadow, and rain-blue accents; gently textured scenery; and simple, high-contrast interface planes. Characters, creature designs, maps, names, dialogue, quest structure, UI composition, animation timing, sound, and gameplay choreography must be independently authored. The functional reference informs only the broad capability of a party-based, turn-based adventure. It must not inform trade dress, screen layouts, menus, copy, world-building, assets, or distinctive sequences.\n\n## Information architecture and navigation\n\nThe shell has a persistent, semantic navigation model. The game view is the primary workspace; panels are temporary layers rather than separate unexplained destinations.\n\n```text\nLaunch / title\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 New game \u2192 accessibility quick setup (skippable) \u2192 tutorial \u2192 town \u2192 dungeon \u2192 ending\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 Continue / Load \u2192 slot picker \u2192 restored safe boundary \u2192 game view\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 Settings \u2192 accessibility, controls, audio, display, language (when supplied)\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 Help & controls \u2192 input-specific action reference\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 Save data \u2192 load, delete-confirmation, recovery status\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 Privacy & diagnostics \u2192 local-data explanation, consent / clear actions\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 PWA status \u2192 install guidance, offline readiness, safe update state\n\nGame view\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 objective / quest panel\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 inventory and party panels\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 pause menu \u2192 save, settings, help, return to title\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 contextual interaction / dialogue / combat layers\n```\n\n- The title exposes only available actions. With no valid save, `Continue` and `Load` are absent or disabled with the accompanying explanation; `New game` remains the primary action.\n- `Escape`, a visible pause affordance, and the mapped gamepad pause action open pause at any safe playable state. Focus loss or tab hiding pauses the game and explains this only once per session.\n- Every panel has a visible title, close control, and a known return target. Closing restores the prior selection and scroll position where feasible. Browser Back never silently discards progress: it closes a transient panel first; leaving the game prompts only when an unsaved, recoverable change would be lost.\n- Modal layers are reserved for blocking choices: save deletion, settings reset, a new-game replacement of an existing active slot, and a recovery choice. They state consequence, affected slot/data, irreversible status, and a safe default (`Cancel`). No timed dialog expires.\n- Navigation labels use player language: `Quest`, `Bag`, `Party`, `Save`, `Settings`, and `Help`. Icons always have adjacent text or an accessible name; an icon alone is never the only cue.\n\n## Story, content, and feedback principles\n\nWriting is concise, warm, and grounded. Dialogue advances in short, skimmable turns: speaker name, one thought or action, then a clear response/continue choice. Quest copy answers **what happened**, **what to do next**, and **where to go** without hiding required direction in decorative prose. The tutorial teaches one action at a time: move/interact, select a combat action and target, observe the result, then save. It never assumes prior genre knowledge.\n\nNarrative presentation gives players control: advance, review the current exchange, and enable captions; it does not auto-advance essential text. A quest update is both spoken/written in the panel and visibly confirmed near the objective. Victory, gained item, blocked route, invalid action, save completion, update-ready, and recovery messages use a combination of short text, an icon or shape, optional audio/haptic feedback where the platform supports it, and a non-blocking visual change. Colour and sound are supplementary, never the sole signal.\n\nCombat is an ordered decision loop: announce whose turn it is, offer legal actions, show required target selection, then resolve with an interruptible/reduced-motion-friendly result and return to the next decision. Illegal or unavailable choices explain why and preserve the current turn. Exploration interactions use an explicit prompt with the action name; locked routes name the missing condition rather than merely refusing movement.\n\n## Layout, visual tokens, and responsive behaviour\n\nThe game scene retains its 2D world view while the interface reflows around it. Essential information is never permanently covered by a decorative frame, cut off by device notches, or dependent on hover.\n\n| Token / rule | Contract |\n| --- | --- |\n| `--surface-base`, `--surface-raised` | Warm parchment/dark-plum interface planes. Body text and essential icons meet at least **4.5:1** contrast; large text (at least 24 CSS px regular or 18.66 CSS px bold) meets **3:1**. |\n| `--text-primary`, `--text-muted` | Primary is used for all essential content. Muted text is never the only carrier of an instruction, state, or warning and meets 4.5:1 when conveying necessary text. |\n| `--accent-action`, `--state-success/warning/danger` | Accent is paired with text and a distinct icon/shape. Focus does not rely on the action colour. Error and destructive states use wording plus iconography. |\n| `--focus-ring` | A high-visibility 3 CSS-px minimum outline with at least 3:1 contrast against adjacent colours; never removed. It has clear offset from the focused control. |\n| Typography | Sans-serif UI type with clear letterforms; text scaling is supported to 200% without clipping, overlap, horizontal page scrolling, or lost actions. Body/default dialogue begins at a readable base size; users may choose larger text and line spacing. |\n| Spacing and targets | Minimum 44 by 44 CSS px target for touch-operable controls, with 8 CSS px separation where adjacent targets could be confused. Targets are not made smaller on compact screens. |\n| Motion | Motion is brief, non-essential, and can be reduced. Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`; provide an in-game reduction setting that removes camera shake, parallax, flashes, auto-panning, and nonessential transitions. No essential timing depends on animation. |\n\n| Viewport | Layout behaviour |\n| --- | --- |\n| Phone / narrow portrait | Full-width world view with safe-area insets. Objective is a compact expandable summary; action controls form a bottom reachable sheet. Inventory, quest, settings, and dialogue become full-screen panels with a sticky close/back control. Combat actions stack or use a single-column selection list; no critical control is below the browser chrome. |\n| Tablet / medium | World stays primary with a side or bottom contextual panel. Combat has a clear action area and target area side-by-side when space allows; otherwise it uses the phone sequence. Panels never overlap the action prompt. |\n| Desktop / wide | Centred game stage with persistent but collapsible objective/status rail. Inventory and quest can use a two-column inspection layout; combat keeps actions and party/enemy status simultaneously visible. Mouse hover may preview a definition but never supplies essential information. |\n\nRotation, resize, zoom, virtual keyboards, and PWA display-mode changes preserve the current game state and selection where practical. If reflow temporarily obscures the selected control, focus moves to the panel heading and a short status message announces the layout change. Full screen is optional and provides an obvious exit path.\n\n## Input and interaction adaptation\n\nAll supported physical inputs invoke one semantic action vocabulary: move, inspect/interact, confirm, cancel/pause, open quest, open bag, open settings, navigate previous/next, and choose a legal combat action/target. A player can complete every core journey without pointer precision, dragging, multi-touch, rapid repetition, or a time limit.\n\n| Surface / input | Required adaptation |\n| --- | --- |\n| Keyboard | Arrow keys and WASD move/navigate where appropriate; Tab and Shift+Tab move through UI controls in visual reading order; Enter/Space confirm; Escape cancels/closes/pause. Avoid keyboard traps; provide an early `Skip to game controls` link from the shell. Key repeat must not confirm a destructive choice or consume multiple turn actions. Control mappings are visible and remappable subject to the later-approved configuration depth; conflicts are explained before saving. |\n| Mouse / trackpad | Click targets match the semantic controls; hover is optional enrichment only. Right-click is not required. The pointer never needs to trace tiny map details to perform a required interaction. |\n| Touch | On-screen controls are reachable, labelled, and may be toggled in settings. Use tap-to-confirm and explicit target selection; do not require pinch, swipe-only navigation, double tap, drag, or long press. A touch action has the same feedback as its keyboard equivalent. |\n| Gamepad | Feature-detect rather than promise a model. Show button glyphs only after detection and accompany them with action text. D-pad/left stick navigates; primary face button confirms; secondary face button cancels; menu button pauses; shoulder buttons may switch top-level panels when discoverable. A disconnected controller preserves state and presents keyboard/mouse/touch alternatives without blocking. |\n| Remote / focus-only devices | These are not a selected delivery target. If a browser presents only directional/confirm/back focus input, the menus use the gamepad-style focus order and all core controls remain reachable; continuous exploration is not promised until a target/device decision is approved. |\n| Voice and other assistive input | Voice command recognition is not collected, enabled, or required in P0. Controls expose standard semantic HTML roles, names, states, and operable buttons so browser voice control, switch control, eye tracking, and other assistive input can target visible actions by label. Canvas/world interactions have equivalent labelled UI prompts and action-list routes. |\n\n## Accessibility policy\n\nThe release target is WCAG 2.2 AA for the public UI and the operable game controls, evaluated with automated checks and manual keyboard, screen-reader, zoom/reflow, touch, and reduced-motion review on the approved browser/device matrix. This is a product quality target; exact assistive-technology combinations remain a release approval gate rather than an invented compatibility claim.\n\n- Use semantic landmarks for banner/title navigation, main game controls, complementary objective/status, and dialogs. Mark decorative art as hidden from assistive technology. Give the world canvas a concise labelled description and provide its essential current state through adjacent semantic status and action elements.\n- Every interactive element has a unique accessible name that matches its visible label where one exists. Examples: `Open quest: Relight the Beacon`, `Use Moss Tonic on Rowan`, `Close inventory`, `Save slot 1`, and `Delete slot 1`.\n- Dialogues announce speaker and text through a controlled, non-interrupting status mechanism; combat announces turn start, selected action/target, damage/healing, and victory/defeat without flooding announcements for decorative animation frames. Notifications are concise, deduplicated, and reviewable in the status/quest panel.\n- Focus is visible at all times, enters a dialog at its heading or first safe action, remains contained only while that blocking dialog is open, and returns to its invoking control when closed. A newly opened non-modal panel receives focus on its heading. Error focus moves to an actionable summary, not an arbitrary visual element.\n- Do not use flicker above three flashes per second. Provide captions/subtitles for all non-text audio that conveys story, instruction, combat state, or warning; identify speaker and relevant sound in concise text. Master audio, music, effects, caption visibility, text size, contrast, and motion settings are reachable before starting a new game and while paused.\n- Required state has a text equivalent: party health uses values and state wording as well as bars; enemy intent uses a label/icon; map interaction, quest progression, and save status use text. Visual settings include a higher-contrast mode and non-colour state markers.\n- Users can pause, slow, or disable nonessential movement and screen effects. No essential dialogue, battle selection, confirmation, error message, or recovery choice disappears by timeout.\n- Settings save independently of campaign saves where storage permits. If persistence fails, keep the in-session choice, state that it will not persist, and preserve a usable default. Reset settings is confirmed and describes the affected preference categories.\n\n## Empty, error, recovery, destructive, and privacy-sensitive states\n\n| Situation | Experience requirement |\n| --- | --- |\n| Empty inventory / no quest / no save | State what is empty, why it may be empty, and the next useful action: e.g., `No items yet\u2014explore the town and finish the first encounter.` No decorative blank panels. |\n| Invalid action, locked exit, unavailable target | Keep the player\u2019s state and turn intact; name the unmet requirement and return focus to the legal choices. Do not use a generic `Error` as the only explanation. |\n| Storage failure, corrupt save, or interrupted save | Never claim a save completed until confirmed. Retain the last valid checkpoint; show retry, return-to-title, and fallback/new-game paths. Quarantined saves are explained as preserved but unusable; recovery text avoids blame. |\n| Offline, install, cache, or update state | Explain whether the current cached version can play, whether an initial download is required, and that an update will wait for a save-safe title/menu boundary. Declining install or update does not block play on a valid cached/current release. |\n| Fault / crash recovery | Present plain-language retry, return to title, and safe-recovery actions. Preserve confirmed progress. A diagnostic option is optional and clearly separate from recovery. |\n| Delete a save | Require a confirmation dialog that names the slot, its progress/time where available, and that deletion is irreversible. Initial focus is `Cancel`; `Delete` is visually and semantically distinct and cannot be activated through a stale/repeated input. Only the selected local slot and associated recovery metadata are removed. |\n| New game over an active slot / reset settings | Explain precisely what will change. New game must use a separate slot or obtain explicit confirmation before replacing a selected slot. Settings reset affects preferences only, not campaign state. |\n| Diagnostics and local data | P0 sends no telemetry. Before any consent-gated local diagnostic record is created or exported, state purpose, included minimal fields, retention, deletion control, and that it does not affect play. `Clear diagnostic data` confirms the local-only effect. Never show save contents or dialogue in diagnostics UI. |\n\n## PWA-specific experience\n\nThe web and installed PWA share the campaign, controls, accessibility settings, semantic UI, and local-save behaviour. Installation is an optional convenience: the title/PWA status area explains availability and has a non-modal fallback when the browser offers no install prompt. Offline status is visible but not alarming. An uncached first visit tells the player that the game cannot begin offline until its assets finish downloading; a known-good installed/cache version continues if an update check fails.\n\nAn update notice appears only at a safe boundary (title or paused menu after a confirmed save) and says whether reloading is needed. It offers `Update now` and `Later`; it never reloads during combat, a save write, a modal choice, or essential dialogue. Cache refresh messaging does not imply that save data was refreshed, deleted, or synchronised.\n\n## Content and interaction review checklist\n\nBefore a content or UI change ships, review it against this contract: original provenance; clear next action and empty/error copy; keyboard, touch, mouse, gamepad, and semantic assistive-input operation; visible focus and accurate accessible names; contrast and non-colour cues; 44 CSS-px touch targets; 200% text/reflow; captions and reduced motion; safe save/update/recovery behaviour; destructive confirmation; and consent/minimisation for any privacy-sensitive interface.\n\n## Open decisions retained for approval\n\n- Exact content quantities, party size, localisation languages, full control-remapping depth, audio scope, and supported browser/device/assistive-technology matrix.\n- The legal, age/parental, regional, and certification policies that may change content warnings or accessibility obligations.\n- Account identity, remote sync, multiplayer, player safety/moderation, live operations, commerce, and analytics. These remain outside the offline P0 experience; no social, payment, reporting, account, or remote-data UI may be designed as committed functionality without approval.\n19:| Casual story player | When I have a short session, help me understand what to do and make visible story progress without complex controls. | Starts, wins the tutorial battle, saves, and resumes a quest. | J1\u2013J4 |\n33:| J6 | Adjust accessibility and feedback: player can make the game usable. | Open settings \u2192 preview/change text, captions, visual and input options \u2192 apply \u2192 preferences persist. | Unsupported option/device is labelled unavailable; reset asks confirmation; settings storage failure leaves current-session setting active and explains it may not persist. No permission denial is required for these settings. |\n59:Input + accessibility \u2500\u2500drives\u2500\u2500> Game shell \u2500\u2500> exploration / UI\n89:### 1. Game shell, session, input, and responsive presentation\n# 02 \u2014 Feature model and release slices\n\n**Inputs:** [domain discovery](00-domain-discovery.md) and the canonical\n[project brief](../PROJECT_BRIEF.md). This document turns only the accepted\noffline-game scope into a model. It records connected and commercial requests\nas approval gates; it does not silently turn them into a first-release\ndependency.\n\n## Product outcome and personas\n\nThe first release is successful when a casual or adult player can start the\noriginal 2D fantasy adventure, complete an understandable first battle, save,\nreturn later without losing confirmed progress, finish the single town and\ndungeon story, and reach its short ending offline after installation or a\nsuccessful first asset download.\n\n| Persona | Job to be done | Success signal | Relevant journeys |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Casual story player | When I have a short session, help me understand what to do and make visible story progress without complex controls. | Starts, wins the tutorial battle, saves, and resumes a quest. | J1\u2013J4 |\n| Adult returning player | When I resume after interruption or a long gap, help me recover safely and understand my current objective. | Restored checkpoint is clear; no confirmed progress is silently lost. | J3, J5 |\n| Player with access needs | When I play on my chosen device, let me read, hear, see, and control the game in a comfortable way. | Can change supported text, caption, visual, and control options before or during play. | J1, J6 |\n| Offline PWA player | When connectivity changes or an update is available, let me keep playing the installed game without corrupting saves. | Cached release runs offline; update waits for a safe boundary. | J1, J5, J7 |\n\n## Core journeys\n\n| ID | Journey and outcome | Normal path | Empty / invalid / denied / offline / conflict / recovery / deletion handling |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| J1 | Start, orient, and configure: player reaches the town and knows the tutorial goal. | Open web game or installed PWA \u2192 choose new game \u2192 optional settings \u2192 readable dialogue and input hints \u2192 town. | No prior save shows New Game; unavailable gamepad falls back to listed keyboard/mouse/touch controls; unsupported input shows a non-blocking message. Offline launch is allowed only when the current assets are cached; otherwise explain that an initial download is needed. Declining optional diagnostics does not block play. |\n| J2 | Learn and win first combat: player understands the turn loop. | Accept first encounter \u2192 choose a legal party action \u2192 resolve enemy turn \u2192 win \u2192 receive reward and quest update. | Empty inventory/action lists show explanation; invalid/stale target or unavailable item is rejected without consuming a turn; defeated party reloads the latest safe checkpoint and explains the consequence. No network permission is needed. |\n| J3 | Explore and advance the campaign: player finishes town, dungeon, and ending. | Talk to characters \u2192 accept quest \u2192 traverse town/dungeon \u2192 resolve required encounter and objective \u2192 claim reward \u2192 see ending. | Locked exits state the missing quest condition; exhausted dialogue has a safe closing line; missing authored reference fails content validation and shows recoverable error rather than breaking state; optional reward absence never blocks completion. |\n| J4 | Manage items and progression: player can use earned resources correctly. | Open inventory \u2192 inspect item \u2192 use/equip only where legal \u2192 see immediate feedback \u2192 close back to play. | Empty inventory has an explicit empty state; invalid use, full/limited capacity (if authored), or ineligible target preserves inventory; quest items cannot be discarded if that would make a required path impossible. Deletion/discard is not a first-release capability unless an authored safe rule is later approved. |\n| J5 | Save, load, and recover: player can leave and return safely. | Manual save or checkpoint completes atomically \u2192 resume chooses latest valid save \u2192 state restores at a safe scene boundary. | No save slot shows explanation; corrupt/incompatible candidate is quarantined, never overwritten, and falls back to the last valid checkpoint or new game; storage denial/quota exposes retry and export/support guidance where feasible; interrupted write keeps prior confirmed save. Local cache and any future remote copy conflict resolve only with explicit player choice; remote sync is not first release. Deleting a save requires confirmation and removes only that selected local save. |\n| J6 | Adjust accessibility and feedback: player can make the game usable. | Open settings \u2192 preview/change text, captions, visual and input options \u2192 apply \u2192 preferences persist. | Unsupported option/device is labelled unavailable; reset asks confirmation; settings storage failure leaves current-session setting active and explains it may not persist. No permission denial is required for these settings. |\n| J7 | Install, update, and recover from a fault: player retains a coherent playable version. | Install when browser allows \u2192 cache approved release \u2192 play offline \u2192 accept update at launch/menu after save boundary. | Installation prompt may be unavailable/declined without blocking web play; offline uncached assets state the requirement; cache refresh failure retains known-good cache; crash/error boundary offers retry, return to title, and safe recovery. Diagnostics are minimal and consent-gated where required; a player can decline or delete local diagnostic data without losing play. |\n\n## Domain vocabulary and state ownership\n\n| Term | Meaning / owner |\n| --- | --- |\n| Campaign | The fixed first-release sequence from new game through ending; owns completion state. |\n| Scene | One authored playable location: town or dungeon; owns exits, encounter zones, and presentation references. |\n| Quest | Authored objective and state machine that gates campaign progress and rewards. |\n| Party | Player-controlled combat group; owns members' current combat-ready values and progression. Exact party size is an authoring decision. |\n| Encounter | A combat instance created from an authored encounter definition; never persists mid-turn. |\n| Item | Authored definition; an inventory stack/reference is the player-owned instance/count. |\n| Save snapshot | Versioned, validated, atomic representation of durable player state at a safe boundary. |\n| Checkpoint | Authored or system-selected safe snapshot point; it is not a promise to restore arbitrary moment-to-moment state. |\n| Content package | Versioned original scenes, dialogue, quests, encounters, items, translations, and audiovisual assets delivered together. |\n\n## System relationship map\n\n```text\nContent package \u2500\u2500validates/defines\u2500\u2500> Scene \u2500\u2500starts\u2500\u2500> Encounter\n      \u2502                                  \u2502                  \u2502\n      \u251c\u2500\u2500defines\u2500\u2500> Dialogue \u2500\u2500updates\u2500\u2500> Quest <\u2500\u2500rewards\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n      \u2502                                  \u2502       \u2502\n      \u2514\u2500\u2500defines\u2500\u2500> Items \u2500\u2500held by\u2500\u2500> Inventory \u2502\n                                                 \u2502\nInput + accessibility \u2500\u2500drives\u2500\u2500> Game shell \u2500\u2500> exploration / UI\n                                                 \u2502\nQuest + inventory + party + scene \u2500\u2500snapshot\u2500\u2500> Save / checkpoint\nSave version <\u2500\u2500compatible-with\u2500\u2500 Content package / PWA release\nPWA cache + release workflow \u2500\u2500protect\u2500\u2500> runnable assets and save boundary\nError recovery + minimal diagnostics \u2500\u2500observe\u2500\u2500> shell, persistence, cache\n```\n\n**Cross-domain invariants and lifecycle boundaries**\n\n- A quest transition, reward grant, and save snapshot are ordered: validate\n  transition, apply reward once, then checkpoint; retrying cannot duplicate a\n  reward.\n- An encounter may read party, item, and quest state but changes durable state\n  only after a resolved turn/encounter safe boundary. A crash cannot restore a\n  half-consumed item or half-applied reward.\n- A scene exit is available only when its authored quest predicate is true.\n  Content validation ensures every required predicate, target, reward, and\n  localisation key exists.\n- Settings affect presentation/input immediately but never campaign rules.\n  The same semantic action must be available through supported keyboard,\n  mouse, touch, and gamepad adaptations.\n- Save snapshots record content/schema version and are written atomically.\n  Cache replacement and application migration happen only outside combat and\n  only while a valid fallback save remains intact.\n- The local offline campaign neither needs identity nor sends player state.\n  Any later account is an optional replication boundary, not campaign truth.\n\n## Accepted domain chapters\n\n### 1. Game shell, session, input, and responsive presentation\n\n**Entities/lifecycle:** `Session` moves `launching \u2192 title \u2192 new-or-resume \u2192\nplaying \u2194 paused \u2192 ending \u2192 title`; `InputAction` is mapped per supported input\nmethod; `ViewportProfile` selects responsive layout. Authoring inputs are title\ncopy, control hints, menu routes, and UI layouts. Rules: pause blocks world and\ncombat advancement; focus loss pauses or reaches a safe state; UI action labels\nremain readable and semantic across screen sizes. Dependencies are accessibility,\nrendering, persistence, and content. Outcome is an understandable, controllable\nstart and return path. Edge cases are no existing save, focus loss, rotation,\nunavailable gamepad, unsupported browser feature, and input remap conflict.\n**First-release boundary:** web/PWA keyboard, mouse, touch, and gamepad\nadaptation; one shared game core. No native-client shell or arbitrary controller\nconfiguration guarantee.\n\n### 2. Exploration, town, dungeon, and campaign content\n\n**Entities/lifecycle:** `Scene` is `unloaded \u2192 entered \u2192 active \u2192 exited`;\n`Exit` is `locked | available | used`; `Interactable` is `available \u2192 used` or\nreusable as authored. Inputs are original tile/layout data, collision shapes,\nspawn points, NPCs, exits, encounter zones, dialogue, and asset references.\nRules: exactly one town and one dungeon form the first campaign; collision and\ngates must leave a completable route. Dependencies are narrative, quests,\ncombat, rendering, and saves. Outcome is readable navigation to the ending.\nEdge cases: blocked exit, empty interaction, absent optional item, and invalid\ncontent reference. **Boundary:** no extra regions, procedural worlds, or shared\nlevels.\n\n### 3. Narrative, quests, onboarding, and ending\n\n**Entities/lifecycle:** `Dialogue` is `available \u2192 shown \u2192 acknowledged`;\n`Quest` is `unavailable \u2192 available \u2192 accepted \u2192 objective-complete \u2192\nclaimed \u2192 completed` (or `failed` only where authored); `TutorialStep` is\n`pending \u2192 presented \u2192 understood`; `Campaign` is `not-started \u2192 active \u2192\ncompleted`. Inputs are original characters, text, localisation keys, objective\npredicates, rewards, and ending sequence. Rules: tutorial teaches a battle and\nsaving before unrestricted progression; required quests cannot be abandoned;\ncompletion is idempotent. Dependencies are scenes, combat, inventory, UI, and\nsaves. Outcomes are clear objectives and a short finish. Edge cases: repeated\nNPC talk, dialogue after completion, missing translation, and an invalid quest\npredicate. **Boundary:** one authored story path; no branching campaign,\nseasonal narrative, or user-authored stories.\n\n### 4. Party combat, encounters, rewards, and balance\n\n**Entities/lifecycle:** `Encounter` is `pending \u2192 active \u2192 player-turn \u2192\nresolution \u2192 won | lost | escaped-if-authored`; `Combatant` is `ready \u2192 acting\n\u2192 resolved \u2192 defeated`; `Reward` is `pending \u2192 granted`. Inputs are party and\nenemy definitions, actions, targeting, encounter placement, reward tables, and\nbalance values. Rules: only legal actions/targets resolve; turn order is visible;\nreward grants once; defeat returns to a safe checkpoint. Dependencies are party,\ninventory, quest transitions, audiovisual feedback, and saves. Outcome is a\nlearnable turn-based first battle and reliable progress. Edge cases: no legal\ntarget, empty item list, invalid action request, pause/focus loss, crash during\nresolution, and stale UI selection. **Boundary:** authored encounters only; no\nmultiplayer, ranked modes, live balance changes, or mid-combat save guarantee.\n\n### 5. Inventory, party progression, and economy\n\n**Entities/lifecycle:** `InventoryEntry` is `absent \u2192 acquired \u2192 usable |\nequipped \u2192 consumed-if-applicable`; `PartyMember` progresses through authored\nstates; `RewardGrant` is `unclaimed \u2192 applied`. Inputs are item definitions,\n\ncodex\n{\"status\":\"pass\",\"summary\":\"The assigned manifest and catalogue records are clear: these are three documentation contracts for SHARD-03, with gates retained and no product implementation or assets. I\u2019m creating only the assigned runbooks using the existing R-series format.\",\"changed_files\":[],\"test_result\":\"\",\"evidence\":{\"agent_log\":\"Reviewed B0009, manifest allocations, catalogue contracts IMP-0021\u2013IMP-0023, and their canonical specification sections.\",\"adapter_log\":\"\",\"test_log\":\"\",\"browser_log\":\"\",\"screenshots\":[]},\"acceptance_results\":[],\"documentation\":{\"reviewed_files\":[\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/PROJECT_BRIEF.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/README.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0009.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0017.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0018.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0019.md\"],\"updated_files\":[],\"summary\":\"Runbook authoring work is in progress.\"},\"known_limitations\":[],\"browser_coverage\":\"Not applicable: this task authors implementation contracts only; it does not add browser behavior.\",\"recommended_next_step\":\"complete\"}\napply patch\npatch: completed\n/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0021.md\n/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0022.md\n/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0023.md\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0021.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0021.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..f363b0f9c00987494fef07146db76dab4e30027f\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0021.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,119 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0021\n+sequence: 21\n+title: Define shared session and safe checkpoint presentation model\n+dependencies: R0004,R0006,R0017\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0005,REQ-0006,NFR-0002,NFR-0003\n+source_specifications: specification/02-feature-model.md#1-game-shell-session-input-and-responsive-presentation,specification/04-experience-contract.md#empty-error-recovery-destructive-and-privacy-sensitive-states\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0021\n+authoring_batch: B0009\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; session and checkpoint contract only.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Define a framework-neutral shared session model for launch, title, new-or-resume,\n+play, pause, ending, focus loss, and confirmed checkpoint presentation. It\n+coordinates the existing campaign and persistence boundaries without owning a\n+persistence driver, platform layout, cache lifecycle, or browser event binding.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0004 supplies safe persistence/checkpoint rules, R0006 supplies recovery\n+behaviour, and R0017 supplies campaign progression and completion state. This\n+contract consumes their stable outcomes; it does not change their ownership.\n+GATE-0003 remains an implementation gate for storage behaviour and GATE-0004\n+remains an implementation gate for concrete campaign assumptions.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `src/app/session/` and `tests/app/session/`.\n+- Session and checkpoint view state, session intents, and safe-boundary API.\n+- Translation of confirmed persistence/campaign outcomes into an honest player\n+  session state.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Model the lifecycle as `launching \u2192 title \u2192 new-or-resume \u2192 playing \u2194 paused \u2192\n+ending \u2192 title`. Expose title actions only when available: without a valid\n+save, Continue and Load are absent or disabled with an explanation while New\n+game remains available. Resume starts only from a validated safe boundary.\n+\n+Pause blocks world and combat advancement. A focus-loss intent safely pauses,\n+or first reaches an existing safe state where immediate pause is unsafe, and\n+records a once-per-session explanation for the presentation layer. Repeated\n+focus-loss, pause, resume, launch, and ending intents are idempotent and may\n+not duplicate rewards, campaign transitions, or save work.\n+\n+Represent checkpoint status separately from a request or in-progress save.\n+Present a checkpoint as confirmed only after R0004 reports successful atomic\n+confirmation. Interrupted, failed, corrupt, or quarantined saves preserve the\n+last valid confirmed checkpoint and surface retry, return-to-title, and\n+fallback/new-game routes supplied by R0006. The session state must never imply\n+that unconfirmed work, an arbitrary combat moment, or remote data can resume.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+Web and installed-PWA adapters consume the same session intents and confirmed\n+checkpoint state. Browser visibility hooks, service-worker/cache refresh,\n+installation prompts, update activation, viewport layout, and storage-driver\n+selection are adapter work and remain outside this shared model. An update may\n+be presented only at an existing save-safe title or paused-menu boundary; this\n+contract does not implement that lifecycle.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not implement browser lifecycle listeners, cache refresh, service workers,\n+new save schemas, storage drivers, network services, account/sync, UI layout,\n+content, assets, audio, or a product gate approval. Do not resolve GATE-0003\n+or GATE-0004.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: session and checkpoint state requires no\n+product visual or source asset. Do not create or reserve maps, sprites, icons,\n+fonts, illustrations, or other assets; `asset_ids` remains blank.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: this contract selects no cue or playback\n+behaviour. Keep audio IDs, brief, duration, loop policy, and style version\n+blank/default; do not create incidental audio.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Use deterministic state fixtures to prove launch/title/new-or-resume/play/\n+  pause/ending transitions and that focus loss cannot advance world or combat\n+  state.\n+- Prove only a persistence-confirmed checkpoint is presented as confirmed;\n+  interrupted, failed, corrupt, and quarantined candidates retain the last\n+  valid boundary and expose the supplied recovery routes.\n+- Run duplicate focus, pause, resume, and completion intents to prove they do\n+  not replay rewards, transitions, or persistence work. Compare metadata,\n+  provenance, requirements, dependencies, and ownership to IMP-0021 and the\n+  manifest while retaining GATE-0003 and GATE-0004.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain state-transition traces, checkpoint-confirmation and recovery fixtures,\n+idempotence results, the manifest/catalogue comparison, and both unresolved\n+gate records.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Session states cover safe launch, title, new-or-resume, play, pause, ending,\n+  and focus-loss behaviour without taking over persistence drivers or layout.\n+- A checkpoint is presented as confirmed only after durable confirmation;\n+  unconfirmed or invalid saves retain safe recovery routes.\n+- GATE-0003 and GATE-0004 remain explicit implementation gates.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0022.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0022.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..3f513a7fd06a425212f181a9600d11c31b103cd9\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0022.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,124 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0022\n+sequence: 22\n+title: Define semantic responsive game-shell and navigation contract\n+dependencies: R0010,R0021\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0007,REQ-0009,REQ-0010,NFR-0004\n+source_specifications: specification/04-experience-contract.md#information-architecture-and-navigation,specification/04-experience-contract.md#layout-visual-tokens-and-responsive-behaviour\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0022\n+authoring_batch: B0009\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; semantic shell and layout contract only.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Define the semantic, responsive web/PWA game-shell contract around the shared\n+session and game state. It specifies labelled navigation, panel/focus routing,\n+viewport profiles, reflow, and non-colour cues without creating a PWA-specific\n+UI, final presentation assets, or fixed device-support claim.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0010 supplies the shared accessibility foundation and R0021 supplies session\n+and checkpoint presentation state. This shell consumes their public states and\n+routes panels to them without changing their APIs. GATE-0002 remains an\n+implementation gate for numeric/browser-device thresholds and GATE-0004\n+remains a gate for final content and layout choices.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `src/app/shell/`, `src/platform/web/layout/`, and `tests/app/shell/`.\n+- Semantic navigation, viewport profiles, and panel/focus routing API.\n+- Title, main controls, status, temporary panels, dialogs, visible focus, and\n+  responsive reflow rules around shared game state.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Provide semantic landmarks for title navigation, main game controls, objective\n+or status, and dialogs. The game view is the primary workspace; Quest, Bag,\n+Party, Save, Settings, Help, privacy/diagnostics, and PWA status are labelled\n+temporary panels with a visible title, close control, and known return target.\n+Icons always have adjacent text or an accessible name. Title actions reflect\n+R0021 availability rather than promising unavailable save actions.\n+\n+Panel changes preserve prior selection and scroll position where practical.\n+Closing returns focus to the invoking control; a newly opened non-modal panel\n+receives focus at its heading. Blocking dialogs describe consequences and use a\n+safe Cancel default. Browser Back closes a transient panel before any leave\n+prompt, and navigation may not silently discard recoverable progress.\n+\n+Define narrow, medium, and wide profiles. Narrow layouts use safe-area-aware\n+world presentation, an expandable objective summary, reachable actions, and\n+full-screen panels with sticky close/back controls. Medium layouts retain a\n+primary world with contextual side or bottom panel; wide layouts use a centred\n+stage with a collapsible status rail and may use two-column inspection. Resize,\n+rotation, zoom, virtual keyboards, and PWA display-mode changes preserve game\n+state and selection where practical; if reflow obscures selection, focus moves\n+to the panel heading and announces the change.\n+\n+Keep visible focus, labels, state text, and non-colour cues available across\n+profiles. Touch-operable controls retain the specified target/separation\n+contract; hover is optional enrichment. Text scaling, contrast, typography,\n+motion, and exact threshold verification remain governed by R0010 and the\n+unresolved GATE-0002 rather than being inferred here.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+The responsive web shell and installed PWA consume the same semantic UI,\n+navigation, session state, and shared campaign rules. PWA display-mode reflow\n+uses the same profiles, not a forked UI. Installation, service workers, cache\n+refresh, update activation, and a final support matrix are outside this\n+contract and remain gated.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not produce final art, fonts, UI assets, campaign content, audio, a fixed\n+browser/device matrix, service-worker behaviour, cache/update implementation,\n+or a duplicate PWA interface. Do not resolve GATE-0002 or GATE-0004.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: semantic shell and layout rules create no\n+visual/source asset. Do not create or reserve icons, fonts, mockups,\n+illustrations, or other product assets; `asset_ids` remains blank.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: this shell contract owns no cue selection,\n+playback, or mix. Keep all audio metadata blank/default and create no audio\n+asset.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Use representative session and viewport fixtures to prove labelled controls,\n+  legal focus order, panel return targets, and safe dialog defaults through\n+  resize and panel changes.\n+- Prove narrow, medium, and wide profiles retain all required controls without\n+  hover-only operation or a PWA-specific UI branch; test reflow focus recovery.\n+- Compare metadata, requirements, provenance, dependencies, and ownership to\n+  IMP-0022 and the manifest; retain GATE-0002 and GATE-0004 without treating\n+  documentation as approval.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain semantic-tree/focus traces, viewport and panel fixtures, PWA/web parity\n+comparison, metadata comparison, and the unresolved gate records.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- The shell supplies semantic navigation, labelled panels, safe dialog and\n+  focus routing, and responsive profiles around shared game state.\n+- Web and installed PWA share one UI contract; no PWA-specific interface,\n+  support-matrix claim, or lifecycle implementation is introduced.\n+- GATE-0002 and GATE-0004 remain explicit implementation gates.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0023.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0023.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..48b3c7e62cdff0dc80b692c295248eed2cae00a7\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0023.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,129 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0023\n+sequence: 23\n+title: Map semantic actions across supported inputs\n+dependencies: R0002,R0021,R0022\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0005,REQ-0009,NFR-0004\n+source_specifications: specification/04-experience-contract.md#input-and-interaction-adaptation\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0023\n+authoring_batch: B0009\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; input semantics only.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Define one semantic input-action vocabulary for web and PWA adapters, covering\n+movement, inspect/interact, confirm, cancel/pause, panels, navigation, and\n+legal combat action/target selection. It makes equivalent actions available\n+across keyboard, pointer, touch, and detected gamepad without creating\n+input-specific rules or committing to unsupported devices.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0002 supplies shared command/revision safety, R0021 supplies safe session and\n+pause intents, and R0022 supplies semantic controls and focus routing. This\n+contract maps physical input to those existing actions and does not alter game\n+rules, persistence, or shell ownership. GATE-0002 remains an implementation\n+gate for approved browser/device compatibility claims.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `src/platform/web/input/`, `src/app/input/`, and `tests/platform/input/`.\n+- Input binding and availability state plus the semantic input-action API.\n+- Repeat, conflict, disconnect, and fallback handling for supported adapters.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Use a single action vocabulary: move, inspect/interact, confirm, cancel/pause,\n+open quest, open bag, open settings, navigate previous/next, and choose a\n+legal combat action/target. Equivalent actions invoke the same command and\n+receive the same state/result feedback. A core journey must not require pointer\n+precision, drag, multi-touch, rapid repetition, or a timeout.\n+\n+Keyboard supports Arrow keys/WASD where appropriate, Tab/Shift+Tab in visual\n+reading order, Enter/Space confirm, Escape cancel/close/pause, and an early\n+Skip to game controls route. Pointer clicks operate the semantic controls;\n+right-click and hover are optional. Touch controls are labelled and reachable,\n+use explicit tap/target confirmation, and do not require pinch, swipe-only\n+navigation, double tap, drag, or long press.\n+\n+Feature-detect gamepad input rather than promising a model. When detected,\n+pair action text with any glyph; map directional navigation, primary confirm,\n+secondary cancel, and menu pause. A disconnect preserves state and supplies\n+keyboard/mouse/touch alternatives without blocking. Focus-only browser input\n+uses the semantic focus order when presented, but continuous exploration on\n+unapproved targets is not promised. Standard semantic roles, names, states,\n+and labelled alternatives expose the same actions to browser assistive input;\n+voice recognition is neither required nor enabled.\n+\n+Repeat handling must be action-aware. Navigation/movement repeat is bounded by\n+the shared command contract; confirm, destructive choices, legal combat\n+actions, and target selection accept one deliberate activation per eligible\n+state/revision. Stale, held, or repeated input may not confirm deletion,\n+consume multiple turns, replay rewards, or bypass a modal Cancel default.\n+Surface remap conflicts before saving, while leaving the approved depth of\n+remapping unresolved.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+The same action vocabulary and adapters apply in responsive web and installed\n+PWA use. Availability may be reported from feature detection, but neither\n+surface promises a controller model or a final browser/device matrix. Native\n+clients, install lifecycle, cache behaviour, and PWA-specific rules are outside\n+this contract.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not implement native clients, voice recognition, arbitrary remapping,\n+input-specific gameplay rules, final support guarantees, UI assets, audio,\n+storage drivers, or product gate approval. Do not resolve GATE-0002.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: input semantics needs no product visual or\n+source asset. Do not create or reserve controller glyphs, icons, illustrations,\n+or other assets; `asset_ids` remains blank.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: this contract selects no cue, playback, or\n+mix. Keep audio IDs, brief, duration, loop policy, and style version\n+blank/default and create no incidental audio.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Use deterministic adapter fixtures to prove keyboard, pointer, touch, and\n+  detected-gamepad events produce equivalent semantic actions and feedback.\n+- Prove held/repeated/stale input cannot duplicate destructive confirmation,\n+  combat selection, rewards, or commands; verify explicit legal-action and\n+  revision checks remain in place.\n+- Prove a gamepad disconnect preserves state and exposes a usable\n+  keyboard/mouse/touch fallback. Compare metadata, provenance, requirements,\n+  dependencies, and ownership to IMP-0023 and the manifest while retaining\n+  GATE-0002.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain cross-input action traces, repeat-safety and stale-input fixtures,\n+disconnect/fallback output, manifest/catalogue comparison, and the unresolved\n+GATE-0002 record.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Keyboard, pointer, touch, and feature-detected gamepad map to equivalent\n+  semantic actions with labelled accessible fallbacks.\n+- Repeat, stale input, and gamepad disconnect cannot duplicate destructive or\n+  turn actions and leave a usable fallback.\n+- GATE-0002, remapping depth, and unapproved target compatibility remain\n+  explicit and unresolved.\n\nhook: PostToolUse\nhook: PostToolUse Failed\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0021.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0021.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..f363b0f9c00987494fef07146db76dab4e30027f\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0021.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,119 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0021\n+sequence: 21\n+title: Define shared session and safe checkpoint presentation model\n+dependencies: R0004,R0006,R0017\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0005,REQ-0006,NFR-0002,NFR-0003\n+source_specifications: specification/02-feature-model.md#1-game-shell-session-input-and-responsive-presentation,specification/04-experience-contract.md#empty-error-recovery-destructive-and-privacy-sensitive-states\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0021\n+authoring_batch: B0009\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; session and checkpoint contract only.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Define a framework-neutral shared session model for launch, title, new-or-resume,\n+play, pause, ending, focus loss, and confirmed checkpoint presentation. It\n+coordinates the existing campaign and persistence boundaries without owning a\n+persistence driver, platform layout, cache lifecycle, or browser event binding.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0004 supplies safe persistence/checkpoint rules, R0006 supplies recovery\n+behaviour, and R0017 supplies campaign progression and completion state. This\n+contract consumes their stable outcomes; it does not change their ownership.\n+GATE-0003 remains an implementation gate for storage behaviour and GATE-0004\n+remains an implementation gate for concrete campaign assumptions.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `src/app/session/` and `tests/app/session/`.\n+- Session and checkpoint view state, session intents, and safe-boundary API.\n+- Translation of confirmed persistence/campaign outcomes into an honest player\n+  session state.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Model the lifecycle as `launching \u2192 title \u2192 new-or-resume \u2192 playing \u2194 paused \u2192\n+ending \u2192 title`. Expose title actions only when available: without a valid\n+save, Continue and Load are absent or disabled with an explanation while New\n+game remains available. Resume starts only from a validated safe boundary.\n+\n+Pause blocks world and combat advancement. A focus-loss intent safely pauses,\n+or first reaches an existing safe state where immediate pause is unsafe, and\n+records a once-per-session explanation for the presentation layer. Repeated\n+focus-loss, pause, resume, launch, and ending intents are idempotent and may\n+not duplicate rewards, campaign transitions, or save work.\n+\n+Represent checkpoint status separately from a request or in-progress save.\n+Present a checkpoint as confirmed only after R0004 reports successful atomic\n+confirmation. Interrupted, failed, corrupt, or quarantined saves preserve the\n+last valid confirmed checkpoint and surface retry, return-to-title, and\n+fallback/new-game routes supplied by R0006. The session state must never imply\n+that unconfirmed work, an arbitrary combat moment, or remote data can resume.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+Web and installed-PWA adapters consume the same session intents and confirmed\n+checkpoint state. Browser visibility hooks, service-worker/cache refresh,\n+installation prompts, update activation, viewport layout, and storage-driver\n+selection are adapter work and remain outside this shared model. An update may\n+be presented only at an existing save-safe title or paused-menu boundary; this\n+contract does not implement that lifecycle.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not implement browser lifecycle listeners, cache refresh, service workers,\n+new save schemas, storage drivers, network services, account/sync, UI layout,\n+content, assets, audio, or a product gate approval. Do not resolve GATE-0003\n+or GATE-0004.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: session and checkpoint state requires no\n+product visual or source asset. Do not create or reserve maps, sprites, icons,\n+fonts, illustrations, or other assets; `asset_ids` remains blank.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: this contract selects no cue or playback\n+behaviour. Keep audio IDs, brief, duration, loop policy, and style version\n+blank/default; do not create incidental audio.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Use deterministic state fixtures to prove launch/title/new-or-resume/play/\n+  pause/ending transitions and that focus loss cannot advance world or combat\n+  state.\n+- Prove only a persistence-confirmed checkpoint is presented as confirmed;\n+  interrupted, failed, corrupt, and quarantined candidates retain the last\n+  valid boundary and expose the supplied recovery routes.\n+- Run duplicate focus, pause, resume, and completion intents to prove they do\n+  not replay rewards, transitions, or persistence work. Compare metadata,\n+  provenance, requirements, dependencies, and ownership to IMP-0021 and the\n+  manifest while retaining GATE-0003 and GATE-0004.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain state-transition traces, checkpoint-confirmation and recovery fixtures,\n+idempotence results, the manifest/catalogue comparison, and both unresolved\n+gate records.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Session states cover safe launch, title, new-or-resume, play, pause, ending,\n+  and focus-loss behaviour without taking over persistence drivers or layout.\n+- A checkpoint is presented as confirmed only after durable confirmation;\n+  unconfirmed or invalid saves retain safe recovery routes.\n+- GATE-0003 and GATE-0004 remain explicit implementation gates.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0022.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0022.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..3f513a7fd06a425212f181a9600d11c31b103cd9\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0022.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,124 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0022\n+sequence: 22\n+title: Define semantic responsive game-shell and navigation contract\n+dependencies: R0010,R0021\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0007,REQ-0009,REQ-0010,NFR-0004\n+source_specifications: specification/04-experience-contract.md#information-architecture-and-navigation,specification/04-experience-contract.md#layout-visual-tokens-and-responsive-behaviour\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0022\n+authoring_batch: B0009\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; semantic shell and layout contract only.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Define the semantic, responsive web/PWA game-shell contract around the shared\n+session and game state. It specifies labelled navigation, panel/focus routing,\n+viewport profiles, reflow, and non-colour cues without creating a PWA-specific\n+UI, final presentation assets, or fixed device-support claim.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0010 supplies the shared accessibility foundation and R0021 supplies session\n+and checkpoint presentation state. This shell consumes their public states and\n+routes panels to them without changing their APIs. GATE-0002 remains an\n+implementation gate for numeric/browser-device thresholds and GATE-0004\n+remains a gate for final content and layout choices.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `src/app/shell/`, `src/platform/web/layout/`, and `tests/app/shell/`.\n+- Semantic navigation, viewport profiles, and panel/focus routing API.\n+- Title, main controls, status, temporary panels, dialogs, visible focus, and\n+  responsive reflow rules around shared game state.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Provide semantic landmarks for title navigation, main game controls, objective\n+or status, and dialogs. The game view is the primary workspace; Quest, Bag,\n+Party, Save, Settings, Help, privacy/diagnostics, and PWA status are labelled\n+temporary panels with a visible title, close control, and known return target.\n+Icons always have adjacent text or an accessible name. Title actions reflect\n+R0021 availability rather than promising unavailable save actions.\n+\n+Panel changes preserve prior selection and scroll position where practical.\n+Closing returns focus to the invoking control; a newly opened non-modal panel\n+receives focus at its heading. Blocking dialogs describe consequences and use a\n+safe Cancel default. Browser Back closes a transient panel before any leave\n+prompt, and navigation may not silently discard recoverable progress.\n+\n+Define narrow, medium, and wide profiles. Narrow layouts use safe-area-aware\n+world presentation, an expandable objective summary, reachable actions, and\n+full-screen panels with sticky close/back controls. Medium layouts retain a\n+primary world with contextual side or bottom panel; wide layouts use a centred\n+stage with a collapsible status rail and may use two-column inspection. Resize,\n+rotation, zoom, virtual keyboards, and PWA display-mode changes preserve game\n+state and selection where practical; if reflow obscures selection, focus moves\n+to the panel heading and announces the change.\n+\n+Keep visible focus, labels, state text, and non-colour cues available across\n+profiles. Touch-operable controls retain the specified target/separation\n+contract; hover is optional enrichment. Text scaling, contrast, typography,\n+motion, and exact threshold verification remain governed by R0010 and the\n+unresolved GATE-0002 rather than being inferred here.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+The responsive web shell and installed PWA consume the same semantic UI,\n+navigation, session state, and shared campaign rules. PWA display-mode reflow\n+uses the same profiles, not a forked UI. Installation, service workers, cache\n+refresh, update activation, and a final support matrix are outside this\n+contract and remain gated.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not produce final art, fonts, UI assets, campaign content, audio, a fixed\n+browser/device matrix, service-worker behaviour, cache/update implementation,\n+or a duplicate PWA interface. Do not resolve GATE-0002 or GATE-0004.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: semantic shell and layout rules create no\n+visual/source asset. Do not create or reserve icons, fonts, mockups,\n+illustrations, or other product assets; `asset_ids` remains blank.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: this shell contract owns no cue selection,\n+playback, or mix. Keep all audio metadata blank/default and create no audio\n+asset.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Use representative session and viewport fixtures to prove labelled controls,\n+  legal focus order, panel return targets, and safe dialog defaults through\n+  resize and panel changes.\n+- Prove narrow, medium, and wide profiles retain all required controls without\n+  hover-only operation or a PWA-specific UI branch; test reflow focus recovery.\n+- Compare metadata, requirements, provenance, dependencies, and ownership to\n+  IMP-0022 and the manifest; retain GATE-0002 and GATE-0004 without treating\n+  documentation as approval.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain semantic-tree/focus traces, viewport and panel fixtures, PWA/web parity\n+comparison, metadata comparison, and the unresolved gate records.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- The shell supplies semantic navigation, labelled panels, safe dialog and\n+  focus routing, and responsive profiles around shared game state.\n+- Web and installed PWA share one UI contract; no PWA-specific interface,\n+  support-matrix claim, or lifecycle implementation is introduced.\n+- GATE-0002 and GATE-0004 remain explicit implementation gates.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0023.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0023.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..48b3c7e62cdff0dc80b692c295248eed2cae00a7\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0023.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,129 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0023\n+sequence: 23\n+title: Map semantic actions across supported inputs\n+dependencies: R0002,R0021,R0022\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0005,REQ-0009,NFR-0004\n+source_specifications: specification/04-experience-contract.md#input-and-interaction-adaptation\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0023\n+authoring_batch: B0009\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; input semantics only.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Define one semantic input-action vocabulary for web and PWA adapters, covering\n+movement, inspect/interact, confirm, cancel/pause, panels, navigation, and\n+legal combat action/target selection. It makes equivalent actions available\n+across keyboard, pointer, touch, and detected gamepad without creating\n+input-specific rules or committing to unsupported devices.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0002 supplies shared command/revision safety, R0021 supplies safe session and\n+pause intents, and R0022 supplies semantic controls and focus routing. This\n+contract maps physical input to those existing actions and does not alter game\n+rules, persistence, or shell ownership. GATE-0002 remains an implementation\n+gate for approved browser/device compatibility claims.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `src/platform/web/input/`, `src/app/input/`, and `tests/platform/input/`.\n+- Input binding and availability state plus the semantic input-action API.\n+- Repeat, conflict, disconnect, and fallback handling for supported adapters.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Use a single action vocabulary: move, inspect/interact, confirm, cancel/pause,\n+open quest, open bag, open settings, navigate previous/next, and choose a\n+legal combat action/target. Equivalent actions invoke the same command and\n+receive the same state/result feedback. A core journey must not require pointer\n+precision, drag, multi-touch, rapid repetition, or a timeout.\n+\n+Keyboard supports Arrow keys/WASD where appropriate, Tab/Shift+Tab in visual\n+reading order, Enter/Space confirm, Escape cancel/close/pause, and an early\n+Skip to game controls route. Pointer clicks operate the semantic controls;\n+right-click and hover are optional. Touch controls are labelled and reachable,\n+use explicit tap/target confirmation, and do not require pinch, swipe-only\n+navigation, double tap, drag, or long press.\n+\n+Feature-detect gamepad input rather than promising a model. When detected,\n+pair action text with any glyph; map directional navigation, primary confirm,\n+secondary cancel, and menu pause. A disconnect preserves state and supplies\n+keyboard/mouse/touch alternatives without blocking. Focus-only browser input\n+uses the semantic focus order when presented, but continuous exploration on\n+unapproved targets is not promised. Standard semantic roles, names, states,\n+and labelled alternatives expose the same actions to browser assistive input;\n+voice recognition is neither required nor enabled.\n+\n+Repeat handling must be action-aware. Navigation/movement repeat is bounded by\n+the shared command contract; confirm, destructive choices, legal combat\n+actions, and target selection accept one deliberate activation per eligible\n+state/revision. Stale, held, or repeated input may not confirm deletion,\n+consume multiple turns, replay rewards, or bypass a modal Cancel default.\n+Surface remap conflicts before saving, while leaving the approved depth of\n+remapping unresolved.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+The same action vocabulary and adapters apply in responsive web and installed\n+PWA use. Availability may be reported from feature detection, but neither\n+surface promises a controller model or a final browser/device matrix. Native\n+clients, install lifecycle, cache behaviour, and PWA-specific rules are outside\n+this contract.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not implement native clients, voice recognition, arbitrary remapping,\n+input-specific gameplay rules, final support guarantees, UI assets, audio,\n+storage drivers, or product gate approval. Do not resolve GATE-0002.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: input semantics needs no product visual or\n+source asset. Do not create or reserve controller glyphs, icons, illustrations,\n+or other assets; `asset_ids` remains blank.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: this contract selects no cue, playback, or\n+mix. Keep audio IDs, brief, duration, loop policy, and style version\n+blank/default and create no incidental audio.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Use deterministic adapter fixtures to prove keyboard, pointer, touch, and\n+  detected-gamepad events produce equivalent semantic actions and feedback.\n+- Prove held/repeated/stale input cannot duplicate destructive confirmation,\n+  combat selection, rewards, or commands; verify explicit legal-action and\n+  revision checks remain in place.\n+- Prove a gamepad disconnect preserves state and exposes a usable\n+  keyboard/mouse/touch fallback. Compare metadata, provenance, requirements,\n+  dependencies, and ownership to IMP-0023 and the manifest while retaining\n+  GATE-0002.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain cross-input action traces, repeat-safety and stale-input fixtures,\n+disconnect/fallback output, manifest/catalogue comparison, and the unresolved\n+GATE-0002 record.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Keyboard, pointer, touch, and feature-detected gamepad map to equivalent\n+  semantic actions with labelled accessible fallbacks.\n+- Repeat, stale input, and gamepad disconnect cannot duplicate destructive or\n+  turn actions and leave a usable fallback.\n+- GATE-0002, remapping depth, and unapproved target compatibility remain\n+  explicit and unresolved.\n\nexec\n/bin/zsh -lc 'python3 projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/validate_runbook_generation.py --wave B0009\ngit diff --check\ngit status --short' in /Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator\n succeeded in 0ms:\nRunbook-generation structural quality gate (not product/release evidence)\ncanonical specification chapters: 13\nspecification provenance links: 44\ncatalogue contracts: 26 (IMP-0001, IMP-0002, IMP-0003, IMP-0004, IMP-0005, IMP-0006, IMP-0007, IMP-0008, IMP-0009, IMP-0010, IMP-0011, IMP-0012, IMP-0013, IMP-0014, IMP-0015, IMP-0016, IMP-0017, IMP-0018, IMP-0019, IMP-0020, IMP-0021, IMP-0022, IMP-0023, IMP-0024, IMP-0025, IMP-0026)\nmanifest contracts: 23 (R0001, R0002, R0003, R0004, R0005, R0006, R0007, R0008, R0009, R0010, R0011, R0012, R0013, R0014, R0015, R0016, R0017, R0018, R0019, R0020, R0021, R0022, R0023)\nR files missing: 0\nblocked contracts: 0\nunverified contracts: 0\nunallocated catalogue contracts: 3 (IMP-0024, IMP-0025, IMP-0026)\nreserved asset IDs: 3 (ASSET-CAMPAIGN-CHARACTERS, ASSET-CAMPAIGN-DUNGEON, ASSET-CAMPAIGN-TOWN)\nbrowser test paths: 0\n M README.md\n m supervisor\n?? projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/\n?? runbooks/.supervisor-children/\n\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0021.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0021.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..f363b0f9c00987494fef07146db76dab4e30027f\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0021.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,119 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0021\n+sequence: 21\n+title: Define shared session and safe checkpoint presentation model\n+dependencies: R0004,R0006,R0017\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0005,REQ-0006,NFR-0002,NFR-0003\n+source_specifications: specification/02-feature-model.md#1-game-shell-session-input-and-responsive-presentation,specification/04-experience-contract.md#empty-error-recovery-destructive-and-privacy-sensitive-states\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0021\n+authoring_batch: B0009\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; session and checkpoint contract only.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Define a framework-neutral shared session model for launch, title, new-or-resume,\n+play, pause, ending, focus loss, and confirmed checkpoint presentation. It\n+coordinates the existing campaign and persistence boundaries without owning a\n+persistence driver, platform layout, cache lifecycle, or browser event binding.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0004 supplies safe persistence/checkpoint rules, R0006 supplies recovery\n+behaviour, and R0017 supplies campaign progression and completion state. This\n+contract consumes their stable outcomes; it does not change their ownership.\n+GATE-0003 remains an implementation gate for storage behaviour and GATE-0004\n+remains an implementation gate for concrete campaign assumptions.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `src/app/session/` and `tests/app/session/`.\n+- Session and checkpoint view state, session intents, and safe-boundary API.\n+- Translation of confirmed persistence/campaign outcomes into an honest player\n+  session state.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Model the lifecycle as `launching \u2192 title \u2192 new-or-resume \u2192 playing \u2194 paused \u2192\n+ending \u2192 title`. Expose title actions only when available: without a valid\n+save, Continue and Load are absent or disabled with an explanation while New\n+game remains available. Resume starts only from a validated safe boundary.\n+\n+Pause blocks world and combat advancement. A focus-loss intent safely pauses,\n+or first reaches an existing safe state where immediate pause is unsafe, and\n+records a once-per-session explanation for the presentation layer. Repeated\n+focus-loss, pause, resume, launch, and ending intents are idempotent and may\n+not duplicate rewards, campaign transitions, or save work.\n+\n+Represent checkpoint status separately from a request or in-progress save.\n+Present a checkpoint as confirmed only after R0004 reports successful atomic\n+confirmation. Interrupted, failed, corrupt, or quarantined saves preserve the\n+last valid confirmed checkpoint and surface retry, return-to-title, and\n+fallback/new-game routes supplied by R0006. The session state must never imply\n+that unconfirmed work, an arbitrary combat moment, or remote data can resume.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+Web and installed-PWA adapters consume the same session intents and confirmed\n+checkpoint state. Browser visibility hooks, service-worker/cache refresh,\n+installation prompts, update activation, viewport layout, and storage-driver\n+selection are adapter work and remain outside this shared model. An update may\n+be presented only at an existing save-safe title or paused-menu boundary; this\n+contract does not implement that lifecycle.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not implement browser lifecycle listeners, cache refresh, service workers,\n+new save schemas, storage drivers, network services, account/sync, UI layout,\n+content, assets, audio, or a product gate approval. Do not resolve GATE-0003\n+or GATE-0004.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: session and checkpoint state requires no\n+product visual or source asset. Do not create or reserve maps, sprites, icons,\n+fonts, illustrations, or other assets; `asset_ids` remains blank.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: this contract selects no cue or playback\n+behaviour. Keep audio IDs, brief, duration, loop policy, and style version\n+blank/default; do not create incidental audio.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Use deterministic state fixtures to prove launch/title/new-or-resume/play/\n+  pause/ending transitions and that focus loss cannot advance world or combat\n+  state.\n+- Prove only a persistence-confirmed checkpoint is presented as confirmed;\n+  interrupted, failed, corrupt, and quarantined candidates retain the last\n+  valid boundary and expose the supplied recovery routes.\n+- Run duplicate focus, pause, resume, and completion intents to prove they do\n+  not replay rewards, transitions, or persistence work. Compare metadata,\n+  provenance, requirements, dependencies, and ownership to IMP-0021 and the\n+  manifest while retaining GATE-0003 and GATE-0004.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain state-transition traces, checkpoint-confirmation and recovery fixtures,\n+idempotence results, the manifest/catalogue comparison, and both unresolved\n+gate records.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Session states cover safe launch, title, new-or-resume, play, pause, ending,\n+  and focus-loss behaviour without taking over persistence drivers or layout.\n+- A checkpoint is presented as confirmed only after durable confirmation;\n+  unconfirmed or invalid saves retain safe recovery routes.\n+- GATE-0003 and GATE-0004 remain explicit implementation gates.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0022.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0022.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..3f513a7fd06a425212f181a9600d11c31b103cd9\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0022.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,124 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0022\n+sequence: 22\n+title: Define semantic responsive game-shell and navigation contract\n+dependencies: R0010,R0021\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0007,REQ-0009,REQ-0010,NFR-0004\n+source_specifications: specification/04-experience-contract.md#information-architecture-and-navigation,specification/04-experience-contract.md#layout-visual-tokens-and-responsive-behaviour\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0022\n+authoring_batch: B0009\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; semantic shell and layout contract only.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Define the semantic, responsive web/PWA game-shell contract around the shared\n+session and game state. It specifies labelled navigation, panel/focus routing,\n+viewport profiles, reflow, and non-colour cues without creating a PWA-specific\n+UI, final presentation assets, or fixed device-support claim.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0010 supplies the shared accessibility foundation and R0021 supplies session\n+and checkpoint presentation state. This shell consumes their public states and\n+routes panels to them without changing their APIs. GATE-0002 remains an\n+implementation gate for numeric/browser-device thresholds and GATE-0004\n+remains a gate for final content and layout choices.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `src/app/shell/`, `src/platform/web/layout/`, and `tests/app/shell/`.\n+- Semantic navigation, viewport profiles, and panel/focus routing API.\n+- Title, main controls, status, temporary panels, dialogs, visible focus, and\n+  responsive reflow rules around shared game state.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Provide semantic landmarks for title navigation, main game controls, objective\n+or status, and dialogs. The game view is the primary workspace; Quest, Bag,\n+Party, Save, Settings, Help, privacy/diagnostics, and PWA status are labelled\n+temporary panels with a visible title, close control, and known return target.\n+Icons always have adjacent text or an accessible name. Title actions reflect\n+R0021 availability rather than promising unavailable save actions.\n+\n+Panel changes preserve prior selection and scroll position where practical.\n+Closing returns focus to the invoking control; a newly opened non-modal panel\n+receives focus at its heading. Blocking dialogs describe consequences and use a\n+safe Cancel default. Browser Back closes a transient panel before any leave\n+prompt, and navigation may not silently discard recoverable progress.\n+\n+Define narrow, medium, and wide profiles. Narrow layouts use safe-area-aware\n+world presentation, an expandable objective summary, reachable actions, and\n+full-screen panels with sticky close/back controls. Medium layouts retain a\n+primary world with contextual side or bottom panel; wide layouts use a centred\n+stage with a collapsible status rail and may use two-column inspection. Resize,\n+rotation, zoom, virtual keyboards, and PWA display-mode changes preserve game\n+state and selection where practical; if reflow obscures selection, focus moves\n+to the panel heading and announces the change.\n+\n+Keep visible focus, labels, state text, and non-colour cues available across\n+profiles. Touch-operable controls retain the specified target/separation\n+contract; hover is optional enrichment. Text scaling, contrast, typography,\n+motion, and exact threshold verification remain governed by R0010 and the\n+unresolved GATE-0002 rather than being inferred here.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+The responsive web shell and installed PWA consume the same semantic UI,\n+navigation, session state, and shared campaign rules. PWA display-mode reflow\n+uses the same profiles, not a forked UI. Installation, service workers, cache\n+refresh, update activation, and a final support matrix are outside this\n+contract and remain gated.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not produce final art, fonts, UI assets, campaign content, audio, a fixed\n+browser/device matrix, service-worker behaviour, cache/update implementation,\n+or a duplicate PWA interface. Do not resolve GATE-0002 or GATE-0004.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: semantic shell and layout rules create no\n+visual/source asset. Do not create or reserve icons, fonts, mockups,\n+illustrations, or other product assets; `asset_ids` remains blank.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: this shell contract owns no cue selection,\n+playback, or mix. Keep all audio metadata blank/default and create no audio\n+asset.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Use representative session and viewport fixtures to prove labelled controls,\n+  legal focus order, panel return targets, and safe dialog defaults through\n+  resize and panel changes.\n+- Prove narrow, medium, and wide profiles retain all required controls without\n+  hover-only operation or a PWA-specific UI branch; test reflow focus recovery.\n+- Compare metadata, requirements, provenance, dependencies, and ownership to\n+  IMP-0022 and the manifest; retain GATE-0002 and GATE-0004 without treating\n+  documentation as approval.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain semantic-tree/focus traces, viewport and panel fixtures, PWA/web parity\n+comparison, metadata comparison, and the unresolved gate records.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- The shell supplies semantic navigation, labelled panels, safe dialog and\n+  focus routing, and responsive profiles around shared game state.\n+- Web and installed PWA share one UI contract; no PWA-specific interface,\n+  support-matrix claim, or lifecycle implementation is introduced.\n+- GATE-0002 and GATE-0004 remain explicit implementation gates.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0023.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0023.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..48b3c7e62cdff0dc80b692c295248eed2cae00a7\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0023.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,129 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0023\n+sequence: 23\n+title: Map semantic actions across supported inputs\n+dependencies: R0002,R0021,R0022\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0005,REQ-0009,NFR-0004\n+source_specifications: specification/04-experience-contract.md#input-and-interaction-adaptation\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0023\n+authoring_batch: B0009\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; input semantics only.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Define one semantic input-action vocabulary for web and PWA adapters, covering\n+movement, inspect/interact, confirm, cancel/pause, panels, navigation, and\n+legal combat action/target selection. It makes equivalent actions available\n+across keyboard, pointer, touch, and detected gamepad without creating\n+input-specific rules or committing to unsupported devices.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0002 supplies shared command/revision safety, R0021 supplies safe session and\n+pause intents, and R0022 supplies semantic controls and focus routing. This\n+contract maps physical input to those existing actions and does not alter game\n+rules, persistence, or shell ownership. GATE-0002 remains an implementation\n+gate for approved browser/device compatibility claims.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `src/platform/web/input/`, `src/app/input/`, and `tests/platform/input/`.\n+- Input binding and availability state plus the semantic input-action API.\n+- Repeat, conflict, disconnect, and fallback handling for supported adapters.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Use a single action vocabulary: move, inspect/interact, confirm, cancel/pause,\n+open quest, open bag, open settings, navigate previous/next, and choose a\n+legal combat action/target. Equivalent actions invoke the same command and\n+receive the same state/result feedback. A core journey must not require pointer\n+precision, drag, multi-touch, rapid repetition, or a timeout.\n+\n+Keyboard supports Arrow keys/WASD where appropriate, Tab/Shift+Tab in visual\n+reading order, Enter/Space confirm, Escape cancel/close/pause, and an early\n+Skip to game controls route. Pointer clicks operate the semantic controls;\n+right-click and hover are optional. Touch controls are labelled and reachable,\n+use explicit tap/target confirmation, and do not require pinch, swipe-only\n+navigation, double tap, drag, or long press.\n+\n+Feature-detect gamepad input rather than promising a model. When detected,\n+pair action text with any glyph; map directional navigation, primary confirm,\n+secondary cancel, and menu pause. A disconnect preserves state and supplies\n+keyboard/mouse/touch alternatives without blocking. Focus-only browser input\n+uses the semantic focus order when presented, but continuous exploration on\n+unapproved targets is not promised. Standard semantic roles, names, states,\n+and labelled alternatives expose the same actions to browser assistive input;\n+voice recognition is neither required nor enabled.\n+\n+Repeat handling must be action-aware. Navigation/movement repeat is bounded by\n+the shared command contract; confirm, destructive choices, legal combat\n+actions, and target selection accept one deliberate activation per eligible\n+state/revision. Stale, held, or repeated input may not confirm deletion,\n+consume multiple turns, replay rewards, or bypass a modal Cancel default.\n+Surface remap conflicts before saving, while leaving the approved depth of\n+remapping unresolved.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+The same action vocabulary and adapters apply in responsive web and installed\n+PWA use. Availability may be reported from feature detection, but neither\n+surface promises a controller model or a final browser/device matrix. Native\n+clients, install lifecycle, cache behaviour, and PWA-specific rules are outside\n+this contract.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not implement native clients, voice recognition, arbitrary remapping,\n+input-specific gameplay rules, final support guarantees, UI assets, audio,\n+storage drivers, or product gate approval. Do not resolve GATE-0002.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: input semantics needs no product visual or\n+source asset. Do not create or reserve controller glyphs, icons, illustrations,\n+or other assets; `asset_ids` remains blank.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: this contract selects no cue, playback, or\n+mix. Keep audio IDs, brief, duration, loop policy, and style version\n+blank/default and create no incidental audio.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Use deterministic adapter fixtures to prove keyboard, pointer, touch, and\n+  detected-gamepad events produce equivalent semantic actions and feedback.\n+- Prove held/repeated/stale input cannot duplicate destructive confirmation,\n+  combat selection, rewards, or commands; verify explicit legal-action and\n+  revision checks remain in place.\n+- Prove a gamepad disconnect preserves state and exposes a usable\n+  keyboard/mouse/touch fallback. Compare metadata, provenance, requirements,\n+  dependencies, and ownership to IMP-0023 and the manifest while retaining\n+  GATE-0002.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain cross-input action traces, repeat-safety and stale-input fixtures,\n+disconnect/fallback output, manifest/catalogue comparison, and the unresolved\n+GATE-0002 record.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Keyboard, pointer, touch, and feature-detected gamepad map to equivalent\n+  semantic actions with labelled accessible fallbacks.\n+- Repeat, stale input, and gamepad disconnect cannot duplicate destructive or\n+  turn actions and leave a usable fallback.\n+- GATE-0002, remapping depth, and unapproved target compatibility remain\n+  explicit and unresolved.\n\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0021.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0021.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..f363b0f9c00987494fef07146db76dab4e30027f\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0021.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,119 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0021\n+sequence: 21\n+title: Define shared session and safe checkpoint presentation model\n+dependencies: R0004,R0006,R0017\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0005,REQ-0006,NFR-0002,NFR-0003\n+source_specifications: specification/02-feature-model.md#1-game-shell-session-input-and-responsive-presentation,specification/04-experience-contract.md#empty-error-recovery-destructive-and-privacy-sensitive-states\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0021\n+authoring_batch: B0009\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; session and checkpoint contract only.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Define a framework-neutral shared session model for launch, title, new-or-resume,\n+play, pause, ending, focus loss, and confirmed checkpoint presentation. It\n+coordinates the existing campaign and persistence boundaries without owning a\n+persistence driver, platform layout, cache lifecycle, or browser event binding.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0004 supplies safe persistence/checkpoint rules, R0006 supplies recovery\n+behaviour, and R0017 supplies campaign progression and completion state. This\n+contract consumes their stable outcomes; it does not change their ownership.\n+GATE-0003 remains an implementation gate for storage behaviour and GATE-0004\n+remains an implementation gate for concrete campaign assumptions.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `src/app/session/` and `tests/app/session/`.\n+- Session and checkpoint view state, session intents, and safe-boundary API.\n+- Translation of confirmed persistence/campaign outcomes into an honest player\n+  session state.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Model the lifecycle as `launching \u2192 title \u2192 new-or-resume \u2192 playing \u2194 paused \u2192\n+ending \u2192 title`. Expose title actions only when available: without a valid\n+save, Continue and Load are absent or disabled with an explanation while New\n+game remains available. Resume starts only from a validated safe boundary.\n+\n+Pause blocks world and combat advancement. A focus-loss intent safely pauses,\n+or first reaches an existing safe state where immediate pause is unsafe, and\n+records a once-per-session explanation for the presentation layer. Repeated\n+focus-loss, pause, resume, launch, and ending intents are idempotent and may\n+not duplicate rewards, campaign transitions, or save work.\n+\n+Represent checkpoint status separately from a request or in-progress save.\n+Present a checkpoint as confirmed only after R0004 reports successful atomic\n+confirmation. Interrupted, failed, corrupt, or quarantined saves preserve the\n+last valid confirmed checkpoint and surface retry, return-to-title, and\n+fallback/new-game routes supplied by R0006. The session state must never imply\n+that unconfirmed work, an arbitrary combat moment, or remote data can resume.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+Web and installed-PWA adapters consume the same session intents and confirmed\n+checkpoint state. Browser visibility hooks, service-worker/cache refresh,\n+installation prompts, update activation, viewport layout, and storage-driver\n+selection are adapter work and remain outside this shared model. An update may\n+be presented only at an existing save-safe title or paused-menu boundary; this\n+contract does not implement that lifecycle.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not implement browser lifecycle listeners, cache refresh, service workers,\n+new save schemas, storage drivers, network services, account/sync, UI layout,\n+content, assets, audio, or a product gate approval. Do not resolve GATE-0003\n+or GATE-0004.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: session and checkpoint state requires no\n+product visual or source asset. Do not create or reserve maps, sprites, icons,\n+fonts, illustrations, or other assets; `asset_ids` remains blank.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: this contract selects no cue or playback\n+behaviour. Keep audio IDs, brief, duration, loop policy, and style version\n+blank/default; do not create incidental audio.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Use deterministic state fixtures to prove launch/title/new-or-resume/play/\n+  pause/ending transitions and that focus loss cannot advance world or combat\n+  state.\n+- Prove only a persistence-confirmed checkpoint is presented as confirmed;\n+  interrupted, failed, corrupt, and quarantined candidates retain the last\n+  valid boundary and expose the supplied recovery routes.\n+- Run duplicate focus, pause, resume, and completion intents to prove they do\n+  not replay rewards, transitions, or persistence work. Compare metadata,\n+  provenance, requirements, dependencies, and ownership to IMP-0021 and the\n+  manifest while retaining GATE-0003 and GATE-0004.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain state-transition traces, checkpoint-confirmation and recovery fixtures,\n+idempotence results, the manifest/catalogue comparison, and both unresolved\n+gate records.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Session states cover safe launch, title, new-or-resume, play, pause, ending,\n+  and focus-loss behaviour without taking over persistence drivers or layout.\n+- A checkpoint is presented as confirmed only after durable confirmation;\n+  unconfirmed or invalid saves retain safe recovery routes.\n+- GATE-0003 and GATE-0004 remain explicit implementation gates.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0022.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0022.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..3f513a7fd06a425212f181a9600d11c31b103cd9\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0022.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,124 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0022\n+sequence: 22\n+title: Define semantic responsive game-shell and navigation contract\n+dependencies: R0010,R0021\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0007,REQ-0009,REQ-0010,NFR-0004\n+source_specifications: specification/04-experience-contract.md#information-architecture-and-navigation,specification/04-experience-contract.md#layout-visual-tokens-and-responsive-behaviour\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0022\n+authoring_batch: B0009\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; semantic shell and layout contract only.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Define the semantic, responsive web/PWA game-shell contract around the shared\n+session and game state. It specifies labelled navigation, panel/focus routing,\n+viewport profiles, reflow, and non-colour cues without creating a PWA-specific\n+UI, final presentation assets, or fixed device-support claim.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0010 supplies the shared accessibility foundation and R0021 supplies session\n+and checkpoint presentation state. This shell consumes their public states and\n+routes panels to them without changing their APIs. GATE-0002 remains an\n+implementation gate for numeric/browser-device thresholds and GATE-0004\n+remains a gate for final content and layout choices.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `src/app/shell/`, `src/platform/web/layout/`, and `tests/app/shell/`.\n+- Semantic navigation, viewport profiles, and panel/focus routing API.\n+- Title, main controls, status, temporary panels, dialogs, visible focus, and\n+  responsive reflow rules around shared game state.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Provide semantic landmarks for title navigation, main game controls, objective\n+or status, and dialogs. The game view is the primary workspace; Quest, Bag,\n+Party, Save, Settings, Help, privacy/diagnostics, and PWA status are labelled\n+temporary panels with a visible title, close control, and known return target.\n+Icons always have adjacent text or an accessible name. Title actions reflect\n+R0021 availability rather than promising unavailable save actions.\n+\n+Panel changes preserve prior selection and scroll position where practical.\n+Closing returns focus to the invoking control; a newly opened non-modal panel\n+receives focus at its heading. Blocking dialogs describe consequences and use a\n+safe Cancel default. Browser Back closes a transient panel before any leave\n+prompt, and navigation may not silently discard recoverable progress.\n+\n+Define narrow, medium, and wide profiles. Narrow layouts use safe-area-aware\n+world presentation, an expandable objective summary, reachable actions, and\n+full-screen panels with sticky close/back controls. Medium layouts retain a\n+primary world with contextual side or bottom panel; wide layouts use a centred\n+stage with a collapsible status rail and may use two-column inspection. Resize,\n+rotation, zoom, virtual keyboards, and PWA display-mode changes preserve game\n+state and selection where practical; if reflow obscures selection, focus moves\n+to the panel heading and announces the change.\n+\n+Keep visible focus, labels, state text, and non-colour cues available across\n+profiles. Touch-operable controls retain the specified target/separation\n+contract; hover is optional enrichment. Text scaling, contrast, typography,\n+motion, and exact threshold verification remain governed by R0010 and the\n+unresolved GATE-0002 rather than being inferred here.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+The responsive web shell and installed PWA consume the same semantic UI,\n+navigation, session state, and shared campaign rules. PWA display-mode reflow\n+uses the same profiles, not a forked UI. Installation, service workers, cache\n+refresh, update activation, and a final support matrix are outside this\n+contract and remain gated.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not produce final art, fonts, UI assets, campaign content, audio, a fixed\n+browser/device matrix, service-worker behaviour, cache/update implementation,\n+or a duplicate PWA interface. Do not resolve GATE-0002 or GATE-0004.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: semantic shell and layout rules create no\n+visual/source asset. Do not create or reserve icons, fonts, mockups,\n+illustrations, or other product assets; `asset_ids` remains blank.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: this shell contract owns no cue selection,\n+playback, or mix. Keep all audio metadata blank/default and create no audio\n+asset.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Use representative session and viewport fixtures to prove labelled controls,\n+  legal focus order, panel return targets, and safe dialog defaults through\n+  resize and panel changes.\n+- Prove narrow, medium, and wide profiles retain all required controls without\n+  hover-only operation or a PWA-specific UI branch; test reflow focus recovery.\n+- Compare metadata, requirements, provenance, dependencies, and ownership to\n+  IMP-0022 and the manifest; retain GATE-0002 and GATE-0004 without treating\n+  documentation as approval.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain semantic-tree/focus traces, viewport and panel fixtures, PWA/web parity\n+comparison, metadata comparison, and the unresolved gate records.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- The shell supplies semantic navigation, labelled panels, safe dialog and\n+  focus routing, and responsive profiles around shared game state.\n+- Web and installed PWA share one UI contract; no PWA-specific interface,\n+  support-matrix claim, or lifecycle implementation is introduced.\n+- GATE-0002 and GATE-0004 remain explicit implementation gates.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0023.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0023.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..48b3c7e62cdff0dc80b692c295248eed2cae00a7\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0023.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,129 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0023\n+sequence: 23\n+title: Map semantic actions across supported inputs\n+dependencies: R0002,R0021,R0022\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0005,REQ-0009,NFR-0004\n+source_specifications: specification/04-experience-contract.md#input-and-interaction-adaptation\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0023\n+authoring_batch: B0009\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; input semantics only.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Define one semantic input-action vocabulary for web and PWA adapters, covering\n+movement, inspect/interact, confirm, cancel/pause, panels, navigation, and\n+legal combat action/target selection. It makes equivalent actions available\n+across keyboard, pointer, touch, and detected gamepad without creating\n+input-specific rules or committing to unsupported devices.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0002 supplies shared command/revision safety, R0021 supplies safe session and\n+pause intents, and R0022 supplies semantic controls and focus routing. This\n+contract maps physical input to those existing actions and does not alter game\n+rules, persistence, or shell ownership. GATE-0002 remains an implementation\n+gate for approved browser/device compatibility claims.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `src/platform/web/input/`, `src/app/input/`, and `tests/platform/input/`.\n+- Input binding and availability state plus the semantic input-action API.\n+- Repeat, conflict, disconnect, and fallback handling for supported adapters.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Use a single action vocabulary: move, inspect/interact, confirm, cancel/pause,\n+open quest, open bag, open settings, navigate previous/next, and choose a\n+legal combat action/target. Equivalent actions invoke the same command and\n+receive the same state/result feedback. A core journey must not require pointer\n+precision, drag, multi-touch, rapid repetition, or a timeout.\n+\n+Keyboard supports Arrow keys/WASD where appropriate, Tab/Shift+Tab in visual\n+reading order, Enter/Space confirm, Escape cancel/close/pause, and an early\n+Skip to game controls route. Pointer clicks operate the semantic controls;\n+right-click and hover are optional. Touch controls are labelled and reachable,\n+use explicit tap/target confirmation, and do not require pinch, swipe-only\n+navigation, double tap, drag, or long press.\n+\n+Feature-detect gamepad input rather than promising a model. When detected,\n+pair action text with any glyph; map directional navigation, primary confirm,\n+secondary cancel, and menu pause. A disconnect preserves state and supplies\n+keyboard/mouse/touch alternatives without blocking. Focus-only browser input\n+uses the semantic focus order when presented, but continuous exploration on\n+unapproved targets is not promised. Standard semantic roles, names, states,\n+and labelled alternatives expose the same actions to browser assistive input;\n+voice recognition is neither required nor enabled.\n+\n+Repeat handling must be action-aware. Navigation/movement repeat is bounded by\n+the shared command contract; confirm, destructive choices, legal combat\n+actions, and target selection accept one deliberate activation per eligible\n+state/revision. Stale, held, or repeated input may not confirm deletion,\n+consume multiple turns, replay rewards, or bypass a modal Cancel default.\n+Surface remap conflicts before saving, while leaving the approved depth of\n+remapping unresolved.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+The same action vocabulary and adapters apply in responsive web and installed\n+PWA use. Availability may be reported from feature detection, but neither\n+surface promises a controller model or a final browser/device matrix. Native\n+clients, install lifecycle, cache behaviour, and PWA-specific rules are outside\n+this contract.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not implement native clients, voice recognition, arbitrary remapping,\n+input-specific gameplay rules, final support guarantees, UI assets, audio,\n+storage drivers, or product gate approval. Do not resolve GATE-0002.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: input semantics needs no product visual or\n+source asset. Do not create or reserve controller glyphs, icons, illustrations,\n+or other assets; `asset_ids` remains blank.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: this contract selects no cue, playback, or\n+mix. Keep audio IDs, brief, duration, loop policy, and style version\n+blank/default and create no incidental audio.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Use deterministic adapter fixtures to prove keyboard, pointer, touch, and\n+  detected-gamepad events produce equivalent semantic actions and feedback.\n+- Prove held/repeated/stale input cannot duplicate destructive confirmation,\n+  combat selection, rewards, or commands; verify explicit legal-action and\n+  revision checks remain in place.\n+- Prove a gamepad disconnect preserves state and exposes a usable\n+  keyboard/mouse/touch fallback. Compare metadata, provenance, requirements,\n+  dependencies, and ownership to IMP-0023 and the manifest while retaining\n+  GATE-0002.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain cross-input action traces, repeat-safety and stale-input fixtures,\n+disconnect/fallback output, manifest/catalogue comparison, and the unresolved\n+GATE-0002 record.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Keyboard, pointer, touch, and feature-detected gamepad map to equivalent\n+  semantic actions with labelled accessible fallbacks.\n+- Repeat, stale input, and gamepad disconnect cannot duplicate destructive or\n+  turn actions and leave a usable fallback.\n+- GATE-0002, remapping depth, and unapproved target compatibility remain\n+  explicit and unresolved.\n\ncodex\n{\"status\":\"pass\",\"summary\":\"Authored R0021\u2013R0023 only, defining gated session/checkpoint, semantic shell/navigation, and cross-input action contracts.\",\"changed_files\":[\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0021.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0022.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0023.md\"],\"test_result\":\"PASS: python3 projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/validate_runbook_generation.py --wave B0009 (0 missing R files; 0 structural errors; 0 unverified contracts). PASS: git diff --check.\",\"evidence\":{\"agent_log\":\"Compared B0009 assignments with manifest R0021\u2013R0023, catalogue IMP-0021\u2013IMP-0023, canonical SHARD-03 specification sections, and established R-series format. All gates remain explicit and unresolved.\",\"adapter_log\":\"\",\"test_log\":\"Structural validator completed successfully for B0009 wave; git whitespace validation passed.\",\"browser_log\":\"Not run: this task creates documentation-only implementation contracts and each assigned manifest record has browser_impact: not_applicable.\",\"screenshots\":[]},\"acceptance_results\":[{\"criterion\":\"Exactly the three assigned R-series files are authored with their manifest mappings.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"Created only R0021.md, R0022.md, and R0023.md. B0009-wave structural validation reported no missing R files and no metadata/provenance errors.\"},{\"criterion\":\"Each output retains gates and has complete provenance and asset/audio metadata.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"Each runbook includes manifest-matched requirements, source specification/catalogue provenance, batch/stages, asset and audio metadata, explicit assessment sections, and unresolved gates.\"},{\"criterion\":\"Structural validation succeeds without overwriting accepted work.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"B0009-wave structural validator exited successfully; files were newly authored at their allocated paths and no existing assigned R0021\u2013R0023 file was replaced.\"}],\"documentation\":{\"reviewed_files\":[\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/PROJECT_BRIEF.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/README.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/02-feature-model.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/04-experience-contract.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0009.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/validate_runbook_generation.py\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0017.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0018.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0019.md\"],\"updated_files\":[\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0021.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0022.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0023.md\"],\"summary\":\"The requested R-series files are the user-facing developer documentation; no README update was needed because no product behaviour, setup, architecture, or progress record changed.\"},\"known_limitations\":[],\"browser_coverage\":\"No task-specific Playwright spec changed: this B0009 task authors implementation contracts only, and all three assigned manifest records declare browser_impact: not_applicable. Browser/visual verification remains for the independent implementation stage.\",\"recommended_next_step\":\"complete\"}\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0021.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0021.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..f363b0f9c00987494fef07146db76dab4e30027f\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0021.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,119 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0021\n+sequence: 21\n+title: Define shared session and safe checkpoint presentation model\n+dependencies: R0004,R0006,R0017\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0005,REQ-0006,NFR-0002,NFR-0003\n+source_specifications: specification/02-feature-model.md#1-game-shell-session-input-and-responsive-presentation,specification/04-experience-contract.md#empty-error-recovery-destructive-and-privacy-sensitive-states\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0021\n+authoring_batch: B0009\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; session and checkpoint contract only.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Define a framework-neutral shared session model for launch, title, new-or-resume,\n+play, pause, ending, focus loss, and confirmed checkpoint presentation. It\n+coordinates the existing campaign and persistence boundaries without owning a\n+persistence driver, platform layout, cache lifecycle, or browser event binding.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0004 supplies safe persistence/checkpoint rules, R0006 supplies recovery\n+behaviour, and R0017 supplies campaign progression and completion state. This\n+contract consumes their stable outcomes; it does not change their ownership.\n+GATE-0003 remains an implementation gate for storage behaviour and GATE-0004\n+remains an implementation gate for concrete campaign assumptions.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `src/app/session/` and `tests/app/session/`.\n+- Session and checkpoint view state, session intents, and safe-boundary API.\n+- Translation of confirmed persistence/campaign outcomes into an honest player\n+  session state.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Model the lifecycle as `launching \u2192 title \u2192 new-or-resume \u2192 playing \u2194 paused \u2192\n+ending \u2192 title`. Expose title actions only when available: without a valid\n+save, Continue and Load are absent or disabled with an explanation while New\n+game remains available. Resume starts only from a validated safe boundary.\n+\n+Pause blocks world and combat advancement. A focus-loss intent safely pauses,\n+or first reaches an existing safe state where immediate pause is unsafe, and\n+records a once-per-session explanation for the presentation layer. Repeated\n+focus-loss, pause, resume, launch, and ending intents are idempotent and may\n+not duplicate rewards, campaign transitions, or save work.\n+\n+Represent checkpoint status separately from a request or in-progress save.\n+Present a checkpoint as confirmed only after R0004 reports successful atomic\n+confirmation. Interrupted, failed, corrupt, or quarantined saves preserve the\n+last valid confirmed checkpoint and surface retry, return-to-title, and\n+fallback/new-game routes supplied by R0006. The session state must never imply\n+that unconfirmed work, an arbitrary combat moment, or remote data can resume.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+Web and installed-PWA adapters consume the same session intents and confirmed\n+checkpoint state. Browser visibility hooks, service-worker/cache refresh,\n+installation prompts, update activation, viewport layout, and storage-driver\n+selection are adapter work and remain outside this shared model. An update may\n+be presented only at an existing save-safe title or paused-menu boundary; this\n+contract does not implement that lifecycle.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not implement browser lifecycle listeners, cache refresh, service workers,\n+new save schemas, storage drivers, network services, account/sync, UI layout,\n+content, assets, audio, or a product gate approval. Do not resolve GATE-0003\n+or GATE-0004.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: session and checkpoint state requires no\n+product visual or source asset. Do not create or reserve maps, sprites, icons,\n+fonts, illustrations, or other assets; `asset_ids` remains blank.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: this contract selects no cue or playback\n+behaviour. Keep audio IDs, brief, duration, loop policy, and style version\n+blank/default; do not create incidental audio.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Use deterministic state fixtures to prove launch/title/new-or-resume/play/\n+  pause/ending transitions and that focus loss cannot advance world or combat\n+  state.\n+- Prove only a persistence-confirmed checkpoint is presented as confirmed;\n+  interrupted, failed, corrupt, and quarantined candidates retain the last\n+  valid boundary and expose the supplied recovery routes.\n+- Run duplicate focus, pause, resume, and completion intents to prove they do\n+  not replay rewards, transitions, or persistence work. Compare metadata,\n+  provenance, requirements, dependencies, and ownership to IMP-0021 and the\n+  manifest while retaining GATE-0003 and GATE-0004.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain state-transition traces, checkpoint-confirmation and recovery fixtures,\n+idempotence results, the manifest/catalogue comparison, and both unresolved\n+gate records.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Session states cover safe launch, title, new-or-resume, play, pause, ending,\n+  and focus-loss behaviour without taking over persistence drivers or layout.\n+- A checkpoint is presented as confirmed only after durable confirmation;\n+  unconfirmed or invalid saves retain safe recovery routes.\n+- GATE-0003 and GATE-0004 remain explicit implementation gates.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0022.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0022.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..3f513a7fd06a425212f181a9600d11c31b103cd9\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0022.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,124 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0022\n+sequence: 22\n+title: Define semantic responsive game-shell and navigation contract\n+dependencies: R0010,R0021\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0007,REQ-0009,REQ-0010,NFR-0004\n+source_specifications: specification/04-experience-contract.md#information-architecture-and-navigation,specification/04-experience-contract.md#layout-visual-tokens-and-responsive-behaviour\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0022\n+authoring_batch: B0009\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; semantic shell and layout contract only.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Define the semantic, responsive web/PWA game-shell contract around the shared\n+session and game state. It specifies labelled navigation, panel/focus routing,\n+viewport profiles, reflow, and non-colour cues without creating a PWA-specific\n+UI, final presentation assets, or fixed device-support claim.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0010 supplies the shared accessibility foundation and R0021 supplies session\n+and checkpoint presentation state. This shell consumes their public states and\n+routes panels to them without changing their APIs. GATE-0002 remains an\n+implementation gate for numeric/browser-device thresholds and GATE-0004\n+remains a gate for final content and layout choices.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `src/app/shell/`, `src/platform/web/layout/`, and `tests/app/shell/`.\n+- Semantic navigation, viewport profiles, and panel/focus routing API.\n+- Title, main controls, status, temporary panels, dialogs, visible focus, and\n+  responsive reflow rules around shared game state.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Provide semantic landmarks for title navigation, main game controls, objective\n+or status, and dialogs. The game view is the primary workspace; Quest, Bag,\n+Party, Save, Settings, Help, privacy/diagnostics, and PWA status are labelled\n+temporary panels with a visible title, close control, and known return target.\n+Icons always have adjacent text or an accessible name. Title actions reflect\n+R0021 availability rather than promising unavailable save actions.\n+\n+Panel changes preserve prior selection and scroll position where practical.\n+Closing returns focus to the invoking control; a newly opened non-modal panel\n+receives focus at its heading. Blocking dialogs describe consequences and use a\n+safe Cancel default. Browser Back closes a transient panel before any leave\n+prompt, and navigation may not silently discard recoverable progress.\n+\n+Define narrow, medium, and wide profiles. Narrow layouts use safe-area-aware\n+world presentation, an expandable objective summary, reachable actions, and\n+full-screen panels with sticky close/back controls. Medium layouts retain a\n+primary world with contextual side or bottom panel; wide layouts use a centred\n+stage with a collapsible status rail and may use two-column inspection. Resize,\n+rotation, zoom, virtual keyboards, and PWA display-mode changes preserve game\n+state and selection where practical; if reflow obscures selection, focus moves\n+to the panel heading and announces the change.\n+\n+Keep visible focus, labels, state text, and non-colour cues available across\n+profiles. Touch-operable controls retain the specified target/separation\n+contract; hover is optional enrichment. Text scaling, contrast, typography,\n+motion, and exact threshold verification remain governed by R0010 and the\n+unresolved GATE-0002 rather than being inferred here.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+The responsive web shell and installed PWA consume the same semantic UI,\n+navigation, session state, and shared campaign rules. PWA display-mode reflow\n+uses the same profiles, not a forked UI. Installation, service workers, cache\n+refresh, update activation, and a final support matrix are outside this\n+contract and remain gated.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not produce final art, fonts, UI assets, campaign content, audio, a fixed\n+browser/device matrix, service-worker behaviour, cache/update implementation,\n+or a duplicate PWA interface. Do not resolve GATE-0002 or GATE-0004.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: semantic shell and layout rules create no\n+visual/source asset. Do not create or reserve icons, fonts, mockups,\n+illustrations, or other product assets; `asset_ids` remains blank.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: this shell contract owns no cue selection,\n+playback, or mix. Keep all audio metadata blank/default and create no audio\n+asset.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Use representative session and viewport fixtures to prove labelled controls,\n+  legal focus order, panel return targets, and safe dialog defaults through\n+  resize and panel changes.\n+- Prove narrow, medium, and wide profiles retain all required controls without\n+  hover-only operation or a PWA-specific UI branch; test reflow focus recovery.\n+- Compare metadata, requirements, provenance, dependencies, and ownership to\n+  IMP-0022 and the manifest; retain GATE-0002 and GATE-0004 without treating\n+  documentation as approval.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain semantic-tree/focus traces, viewport and panel fixtures, PWA/web parity\n+comparison, metadata comparison, and the unresolved gate records.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- The shell supplies semantic navigation, labelled panels, safe dialog and\n+  focus routing, and responsive profiles around shared game state.\n+- Web and installed PWA share one UI contract; no PWA-specific interface,\n+  support-matrix claim, or lifecycle implementation is introduced.\n+- GATE-0002 and GATE-0004 remain explicit implementation gates.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0023.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0023.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..48b3c7e62cdff0dc80b692c295248eed2cae00a7\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0023.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,129 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0023\n+sequence: 23\n+title: Map semantic actions across supported inputs\n+dependencies: R0002,R0021,R0022\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0005,REQ-0009,NFR-0004\n+source_specifications: specification/04-experience-contract.md#input-and-interaction-adaptation\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0023\n+authoring_batch: B0009\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; input semantics only.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Define one semantic input-action vocabulary for web and PWA adapters, covering\n+movement, inspect/interact, confirm, cancel/pause, panels, navigation, and\n+legal combat action/target selection. It makes equivalent actions available\n+across keyboard, pointer, touch, and detected gamepad without creating\n+input-specific rules or committing to unsupported devices.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0002 supplies shared command/revision safety, R0021 supplies safe session and\n+pause intents, and R0022 supplies semantic controls and focus routing. This\n+contract maps physical input to those existing actions and does not alter game\n+rules, persistence, or shell ownership. GATE-0002 remains an implementation\n+gate for approved browser/device compatibility claims.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `src/platform/web/input/`, `src/app/input/`, and `tests/platform/input/`.\n+- Input binding and availability state plus the semantic input-action API.\n+- Repeat, conflict, disconnect, and fallback handling for supported adapters.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Use a single action vocabulary: move, inspect/interact, confirm, cancel/pause,\n+open quest, open bag, open settings, navigate previous/next, and choose a\n+legal combat action/target. Equivalent actions invoke the same command and\n+receive the same state/result feedback. A core journey must not require pointer\n+precision, drag, multi-touch, rapid repetition, or a timeout.\n+\n+Keyboard supports Arrow keys/WASD where appropriate, Tab/Shift+Tab in visual\n+reading order, Enter/Space confirm, Escape cancel/close/pause, and an early\n+Skip to game controls route. Pointer clicks operate the semantic controls;\n+right-click and hover are optional. Touch controls are labelled and reachable,\n+use explicit tap/target confirmation, and do not require pinch, swipe-only\n+navigation, double tap, drag, or long press.\n+\n+Feature-detect gamepad input rather than promising a model. When detected,\n+pair action text with any glyph; map directional navigation, primary confirm,\n+secondary cancel, and menu pause. A disconnect preserves state and supplies\n+keyboard/mouse/touch alternatives without blocking. Focus-only browser input\n+uses the semantic focus order when presented, but continuous exploration on\n+unapproved targets is not promised. Standard semantic roles, names, states,\n+and labelled alternatives expose the same actions to browser assistive input;\n+voice recognition is neither required nor enabled.\n+\n+Repeat handling must be action-aware. Navigation/movement repeat is bounded by\n+the shared command contract; confirm, destructive choices, legal combat\n+actions, and target selection accept one deliberate activation per eligible\n+state/revision. Stale, held, or repeated input may not confirm deletion,\n+consume multiple turns, replay rewards, or bypass a modal Cancel default.\n+Surface remap conflicts before saving, while leaving the approved depth of\n+remapping unresolved.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+The same action vocabulary and adapters apply in responsive web and installed\n+PWA use. Availability may be reported from feature detection, but neither\n+surface promises a controller model or a final browser/device matrix. Native\n+clients, install lifecycle, cache behaviour, and PWA-specific rules are outside\n+this contract.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not implement native clients, voice recognition, arbitrary remapping,\n+input-specific gameplay rules, final support guarantees, UI assets, audio,\n+storage drivers, or product gate approval. Do not resolve GATE-0002.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: input semantics needs no product visual or\n+source asset. Do not create or reserve controller glyphs, icons, illustrations,\n+or other assets; `asset_ids` remains blank.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: this contract selects no cue, playback, or\n+mix. Keep audio IDs, brief, duration, loop policy, and style version\n+blank/default and create no incidental audio.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Use deterministic adapter fixtures to prove keyboard, pointer, touch, and\n+  detected-gamepad events produce equivalent semantic actions and feedback.\n+- Prove held/repeated/stale input cannot duplicate destructive confirmation,\n+  combat selection, rewards, or commands; verify explicit legal-action and\n+  revision checks remain in place.\n+- Prove a gamepad disconnect preserves state and exposes a usable\n+  keyboard/mouse/touch fallback. Compare metadata, provenance, requirements,\n+  dependencies, and ownership to IMP-0023 and the manifest while retaining\n+  GATE-0002.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain cross-input action traces, repeat-safety and stale-input fixtures,\n+disconnect/fallback output, manifest/catalogue comparison, and the unresolved\n+GATE-0002 record.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Keyboard, pointer, touch, and feature-detected gamepad map to equivalent\n+  semantic actions with labelled accessible fallbacks.\n+- Repeat, stale input, and gamepad disconnect cannot duplicate destructive or\n+  turn actions and leave a usable fallback.\n+- GATE-0002, remapping depth, and unapproved target compatibility remain\n+  explicit and unresolved.\n\ntokens used\n48,921\n", "adapter_log": "", "test_log": "Structural validator completed successfully for B0009 wave; git whitespace validation passed.", "browser_log": "Not run: this task creates documentation-only implementation contracts and each assigned manifest record has browser_impact: not_applicable.", "screenshots": []}, "acceptance_results": [{"criterion": "Exactly the three assigned R-series files are authored with their manifest mappings.", "status": "pass", "evidence": "Created only R0021.md, R0022.md, and R0023.md. B0009-wave structural validation reported no missing R files and no metadata/provenance errors."}, {"criterion": "Each output retains gates and has complete provenance and asset/audio metadata.", "status": "pass", "evidence": "Each runbook includes manifest-matched requirements, source specification/catalogue provenance, batch/stages, asset and audio metadata, explicit assessment sections, and unresolved gates."}, {"criterion": "Structural validation succeeds without overwriting accepted work.", "status": "pass", "evidence": "B0009-wave structural validator exited successfully; files were newly authored at their allocated paths and no existing assigned R0021\u2013R0023 file was replaced."}], "documentation": {"reviewed_files": ["projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/PROJECT_BRIEF.md", "projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/README.md", "projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/02-feature-model.md", "projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/04-experience-contract.md", "projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0009.md", "projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json", "projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json", "projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/validate_runbook_generation.py", "projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0017.md", "projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0018.md", "projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0019.md"], "updated_files": ["projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0021.md", "projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0022.md", "projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0023.md"], "summary": "The requested R-series files are the user-facing developer documentation; no README update was needed because no product behaviour, setup, architecture, or progress record changed."}, "known_limitations": [], "browser_coverage": "No task-specific Playwright spec changed: this B0009 task authors implementation contracts only, and all three assigned manifest records declare brow